  "title": "Ziyarat of Imam Ali al-Reza (a.s.) — Other Forms",
  "data": "From al-Kitab al-Atiq al-Gharawi\nWhen you set out from home for the ziyarat, recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِلَيْكَ اَخْرُجُ وَاِلَيْكَ اَتَوَجَّهُ\nALLAAHUMMA ILAYKA AKHRUJU WA ILAYKA ATAWAJJAH\nO Allah, to You I go forth and to You I turn;\nوَبِكَ اٰمَنْتُ وَعَلَيْكَ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَبِكَ اسْتَعَنْتُ\nWA BIKA AAMANTU WA A'LAYKA TAWAKKALTU WA BIKAS TA'ANT\nin You I believe, on You I rely, and from You I seek help.\nوَاِلٰى مَشَاهِدِ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ وَاَصْفِيَاۤئِكَ قَصَدْتُ\nWA ILAA MASHAAHIDI AWLIYAA'IKA WA ASFIYAA'IKA QASADT\nTo the shrines of Your friends and Your chosen ones I make my way,\nوَاِلَيْكَ رَغِبْتُ\nWA ILAYKA RAGHIBT\nand for You I long.\nفَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nFASALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADINIT TAAHIREEN\nSo bless Muhammad and the pure family of Muhammad,\nوَبَلِّغْنِيْ اَمَلِيْ وَرَجَاۤئِيْ فِيْ زِيَارَتِيْ اِيَّاهُمْ وَقَصْدِيْ اِلَيْهِمْ\nWA BALLIGHNEE AMALEE WA RAJAA'EE FEE ZIYAARATEE IYYAAHUM WA QASDEE ILAYHIM\nand bring me to what I hope and wish for in visiting them and setting out towards them,\nفِيْ خَيْرٍ وَعَافِيَةٍ وَسِتْرٍ وَسَلَامَةٍ وَاَمْنٍ وَكِفَايَةٍ\nFEE KHAYRIN WA A'AFIYATIN WA SITRIN WA SALAAMATIN WA AMNIN WA KIFAAYAH\nin goodness and well-being, under Your cover, in safety, security and sufficiency.\nوَرُدَّنِيْ مَقْبُوْلًا مَبْرُوْرًا مَاْجُوْرًا مَوْفُوْرًا سَعِيْدًا غَانِمًا\nWA RUDDANEE MAQBOOLAN MABROORAN MA'JOORAN MAWFOORAN SA'EEDAN GHAANIMAA\nBring me back accepted, approved and rewarded, with an abundant share, happy and having gained,\nوَارْزُقْنِي الْعَوْدَ\nWARZUQNIL A'WD\nand grant me to return.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَاۤ اَبْقَيْتَنِيْ فَلَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ لِزِيَارَةِ مَشَاهِدِهِمْ وَمَعَارِجِهِمْ\nALLAAHUMMA MAA ABQAYTANEE FALAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI LIZIYAARATI MASHAAHIDIHIM WA MA'AARIJIHIM\nO Allah, for as long as You keep me alive, do not make this my last visit to their shrines and the places of their ascent;\nاِنَّكَ اَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nINNAKA ARHAMUR RAAHIMEEN\nsurely You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.\nWhen you arrive, perform ghusl. On the way, glorify, praise and magnify Allah often; the best and most complete words are:\nسُبْحَانَ اللّٰهِ وَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَاللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nSUBHAANALLAAHI WAL HAMDU LILLAAHI WA LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WALLAAHU AKBAR\nGlory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest;\nلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nLAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nthere is no might and no strength except through Allah, the High, the Great.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ النَّبِيِّ وَعَلٰۤى اٰلِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ وَسَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADININ NABIYYI WA A'LAA AALIHIT TAYYIBEENAT TAAHIREENA WA SALLAMA TASLEEMAA\nMay Allah bless Muhammad the Prophet and his good and pure family, and grant them abundant peace.\nWhen you reach the tomb, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَلَمُ الْهَادِيْ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'LAMUL HAADEE\nPeace be upon you, O guiding sign.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْوَصِيُّ الزَّكِيُّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL WASIYYUZ ZAKIYY\nPeace be upon you, O pure successor.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْاِمَامُ الْبَرُّ التَّقِيُّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL IMAAMUL BARRUT TAQIYY\nPeace be upon you, O righteous and God-fearing Imam.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَلَمُ الْمُطَهَّرُ مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'LAMUL MUTAHHARU MINADH DHUNOOB\nPeace be upon you, O sign purified of sins.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وِعَاۤءَ حُكْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WI'AA'A HUKMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O vessel of Allah’s wisdom.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَيْبَةَ سِرِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'YBATA SIRRILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O keeper of Allah’s secret.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْحَافِظُ لِوَحْيِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL HAAFIZU LIWAHYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O guardian of Allah’s revelation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُسْتَوْفِيْ فِيْ طَاعَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUSTAWFEE FEE TAA'ATILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who were complete in obedience to Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُتَرْجِمُ لِكِتَابِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUTARJIMU LIKITAABILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O interpreter of the Book of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الدَّاعِيْ اِلٰى تَوْحِيْدِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAD DAA'EE ILAA TAWHEEDILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O caller to the Oneness of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُعَبِّرُ لِمُرَادِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MU'ABBIRU LIMURAADILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O expounder of what Allah intends.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُحَلِّلُ لِحَلَالِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمُحَرِّمُ لِحَرَامِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUHALLILU LIHALAALILLAAHI WAL MUHARRIMU LIHARAAMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who made lawful what Allah made lawful and forbade what Allah forbade,\nوَالدَّاعِيْ اِلٰى دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ وَالْمُعْلِنُ لِاَحْكَامِ اللّٰهِ\nWAD DAA'EE ILAA DEENILLAAHI WAL MU'LINU LI-AHKAAMILLAAH\nwho called to the religion of Allah and proclaimed the laws of Allah,\nوَالْفَاحِصُ عَنْ مَعْرِفَةِ اللّٰهِ\nWAL FAAHISU A'N MA'RIFATILLAAH\nand searched out the knowledge of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا الْحَسَنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAL HASAN\nPeace be upon you, O Abu al-Hasan.\nاَشْهَدُ يَا مَوْلَايَ اَنَّكَ حُجَّةُ اللّٰهِ وَاَمِيْنُهٗ\nASH-HADU YAA MAWLAAYA ANNAKA HUJJATULLAAHI WA AMEENUH\nI bear witness, O my master, that you are the proof of Allah and His trustee,\nوَصَفْوَةُ اللّٰهِ وَحَبِيْبُهٗ\nWA SAFWATULLAAHI WA HABEEBUH\nthe chosen one of Allah and His beloved,\nوَخِيَرَةُ اللّٰهِ مِنْ خَلْقِهٖ وَحُجَّتُهٗ عَلٰى عِبَادِهٖ\nWA KHIYARATULLAAHI MIN KHALQIHEE WA HUJJATUHOO A'LAA I'BAADIH\nthe best of Allah’s creation and His proof over His servants.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّهٗ مَنْ وَالَاكَ فَقَدْ وَالَى اللّٰهَ\nASH-HADU ANNAHOO MAN WAALAAKA FAQAD WAALALLAAH\nI bear witness that whoever is loyal to you is loyal to Allah,\nوَمَنْ عَادَاكَ فَقَدْ عَادَى اللّٰهَ\nWA MAN A'ADAAKA FAQAD A'ADALLAAH\nwhoever is hostile to you is hostile to Allah,\nوَمَنِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِكَ وَبِالْاَئِمَّةِ مِنْ اٰبَاۤئِكَ وَوُلْدِكَ فَقَدِ اسْتَمْسَكَ بِالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقٰى\nWA MANIS TAMSAKA BIKA WA BIL A'IMMATI MIN AABAA'IKA WA WULDIKA FAQADIS TAMSAKA BIL U'RWATIL WUTHQAA\nand whoever holds fast to you and to the Imams among your forefathers and your descendants has held fast to the firmest handle.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ كَلِمَةُ التَّقْوٰى وَاَعْلَامُ الْهُدٰى وَنُوْرٌ لِسَاۤئِرِ الْوَرٰى\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKUM KALIMATUT TAQWAA WA A'LAAMUL HUDAA WA NOORUN LISAA'IRIL WARAA\nAnd I bear witness that you are the word of piety, the signs of guidance and a light for all creatures.\nThen lean over the tomb, kiss it and recite:\nبِاَبِيْ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ الشَّهِيْدُ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE AYYUHAS SIDDEEQUSH SHAHEED\nMay my father and mother be your ransom, O truthful one, O martyr.\nبِاَبِيْ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْ يَا ابْنَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَسَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ وَاِمَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE YABNA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA SAYYIDIL WASIYYEENA WA IMAAMIL MUSLIMEEN\nMay my father and mother be your ransom, O son of Amir al-Mu’minin, master of the successors and Imam of the Muslims,\nوَحُجَّةِ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الْخَلْقِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA HUJJATILLAAHI A'LAL KHALQI AJMA'EEN\nand proof of Allah over all creation.\nPray two units at the tomb. When you have finished and wish to bid him farewell, recite:\nيَا مَوْلَايَ يَاۤ اَبَا الْحَسَنِ يَا مَوْلَايَ اَيُّهَا الرِّضَا\nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA ABAL HASANI YAA MAWLAAYA AYYUHAR RIDAA\nO my master, O Abu al-Hasan! O my master, O al-Rida!\nاَتَيْتُكَ زَاۤئِرًا\nATAYTUKA ZAA'IRAA\nI have come to you as a visitor,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ خَيْرُ مَزُوْرٍ بَعْدَ اٰبَاۤئِكَ وَاَفْضَلُ مَقْصُوْدٍ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA KHAYRU MAZOORIN BA'DA AABAA'IKA WA AFDALU MAQSOOD\nand I bear witness that you are the best to be visited after your forefathers and the most excellent to be sought.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مَنْ زَارَكَ فَقَدْ وَصَلَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MAN ZAARAKA FAQAD WASALA RASOOLALLAAH\nI bear witness that whoever visits you has kept his bond with the Messenger of Allah,\nوَاَبْهَجَ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةَ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA ABHAJA FAATIMATA SAYYIDATA NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nhas gladdened Fatimah, mistress of the women of the worlds,\nوَنَالَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْفَوْزَ الْعَظِيْمَ\nWA NAALA MINALLAAHIL FAWZAL A'ZEEM\nand has attained from Allah the great triumph.\nفَلَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِكَ وَاِتْيَانِ مَشْهَدِكَ\nFALAA JA'ALAHULLAAHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN ZIYAARATIKA WA ITYAANI MASH-HADIK\nMay Allah not make this my last visit to you and my last coming to your shrine;\nوَرَزَقَنِيَ الْعَوْدَ ثُمَّ الْعَوْدَ اِلَيْكَ\nWA RAZAQANIYAL A'WDA THUMMAL A'WDA ILAYK\nmay He grant me to return to you again and again.\nاٰمِيْنَ رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAAMEENA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nAmen, Lord of the worlds.",
  "tabs": [
    "From Rawdat al-Adhkar\nPerform the ghusl of ziyarat. When the dome comes into sight, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَاۤ اَهْلَ بَيْتِ النُّبُوَّةِ وَمَعْدِنَ الرِّسَالَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA AHLA BAYTIN NUBUWWATI WA MA'DINAR RISAALAH\nPeace be upon you, O Household of prophethood and mine of the divine message,\nوَخُزَّانَ الْعِلْمِ وَمُنْتَهَى الْحِلْمِ وَاُصُوْلَ الْكَرَمِ\nWA KHUZZAANAL I'LMI WA MUNTAHAL HILMI WA USOOLAL KARAM\ntreasurers of knowledge, utmost in forbearance, roots of generosity,\nوَقَادَةَ الْاُمَمِ وَسُلْطَانَ الْعِبَادِ وَدَعَاۤئِمَ الْاَخْيَارِ\nWA QAADATAL UMAMI WA SULTAANAL I'BAADI WA DA'AA'IMAL AKHYAAR\nleaders of the nations, rulers of the servants, pillars of the good,\nوَعَنَاصِرَ الْاَبْرَارِ وَمَنَاصَّةَ الْعِبَادِ وَاَرْكَانَ الْبِلَادِ\nWA A'NAASIRAL ABRAARI WA MANAASSATAL I'BAADI WA ARKAANAL BILAAD\nfoundations of the righteous, support of the servants and mainstays of the lands,\nوَاَبْوَابَ الْاِيْمَانِ وَاُمَنَاۤءَ الرَّحْمٰنِ\nWA ABWAABAL EEMAANI WA UMANAA'AR RAHMAAN\ndoors of faith and trustees of the All-beneficent,\nوَسُلَالَةَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ وَصَفْوَةَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nWA SULAALATAN NABIYYEENA WA SAFWATAL MURSALEEN\ndescendants of the prophets, the choice of the messengers,\nوَعِتْرَةَ خِيَرَةِ رَسُوْلِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA I'TRATA KHIYARATI RASOOLI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nand the family of the chosen Messenger of the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nAt the door of the shrine, ask permission to enter:\nيَا مَوْلَايَ وَابْنَ مَوْلَايَ\nYAA MAWLAAYA WABNA MAWLAAY\nO my master and son of my master,\nاَنَا عَبْدُكَ وَابْنُ عَبْدِكَ الذَّلِيْلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ الْمُعْتَرِفُ بِحَقِّكَ\nANAA A'BDUKA WABNU A'BDIKADH DHALEELU BAYNA YADAYKAL MU'TARIFU BIHAQQIK\nI am your servant and the son of your servant, humbled before you, acknowledging your right.\nجَاۤءَكَ مُسْتَجِيْرًا بِذِمَّتِكَ قَاصِدًا لِحَرَمِكَ\nJAA'AKA MUSTAJEERAN BIDHIMMATIKA QAASIDAN LIHARAMIK\nHe has come to you seeking the shelter of your protection, making for your sanctuary,\nمُتَوَجِّهًا لِمَقَامِكَ مُتَوَسِّلًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِكَ\nMUTAWAJJIHAN LIMAQAAMIKA MUTAWASSILAN ILALLAAHI BIK\nturning to your station and seeking a means to Allah through you.\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا اللّٰهُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA ALLAAH\nMay I enter, O Allah?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nA'ADKHULU YAA RASOOLALLAAH\nMay I enter, O Messenger of Allah?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَاۤ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nA'ADKHULU YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEEN\nMay I enter, O Amir al-Mu’minin?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا فَاطِمَةُ الزَّهْرَاۤءُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA FAATIMATUZ ZAHRAA'\nMay I enter, O Fatimah al-Zahra?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا حَسَنُ الْمُجْتَبٰى\nA'ADKHULU YAA HASANUL MUJTABAA\nMay I enter, O Hasan al-Mujtaba?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا حُسَيْنُ الشَّهِيْدُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA HUSAYNUSH SHAHEED\nMay I enter, O Husayn the martyr?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا زَيْنَ الْعَابِدِيْنَ\nA'ADKHULU YAA ZAYNAL A'ABIDEEN\nMay I enter, O Zayn al-Abidin?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا مُحَمَّدُ الْبَاقِرُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA MUHAMMADUL BAAQIR\nMay I enter, O Muhammad al-Baqir?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا جَعْفَرُ الصَّادِقُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA JA'FARUS SAADIQ\nMay I enter, O Ja’far al-Sadiq?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا مُوْسَى الْكَاظِمُ\nA'ADKHULU YAA MOOSAL KAAZIM\nMay I enter, O Musa al-Kazim?\nءَاَدْخُلُ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nA'ADKHULU YAA HUJJATALLAAH\nMay I enter, O proof of Allah?\nءَاَدْخُلُ اَيَّتُهَا الْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ الْمُحْدِقُوْنَ فِيْ هٰذَا الْمَشْهَدِ\nA'ADKHULU AYYATUHAL MALAA'IKATUL MUHDIQOONA FEE HAADHAL MASH-HAD\nMay I enter, O angels who surround this shrine?\nعَلَيْكَ سَلَامُ اللّٰهِ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَابْنَ مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nA'LAYKA SALAAMULLAAHI YAA MAWLAAYA WABNA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nUpon you be the peace of Allah, O my master and son of my master, and His mercy and blessings.\nEnter with your right foot first, reciting:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ وَبِاللّٰهِ عَلٰى مِلَّةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nBISMILLAAHI WA BILLAAHI A'LAA MILLATI RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nIn the name of Allah and by Allah, on the creed of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and his family.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ وَاَنَّ عَلِيًّا وَلِيُّ اللّٰهِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUHOO WA ANNA A'LIYYAN WALIYYULLAAH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and that Ali is the friend of Allah.\nStand before the tomb and make the intention of the ziyarat of Imam al-Reza (a.s.) for yourself, your parents and forefathers, your relatives and all believing men and women. Then recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ وَلِيِّهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYAA ALLAAHI WABNA WALIYYIH\nPeace be upon you, O friend of Allah and son of His friend.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ حُجَّتِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAHI WABNA HUJJATIH\nPeace be upon you, O proof of Allah and son of His proof.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ فِيْ ظُلُمَاتِ الْاَرْضِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA NOORALLAAHI FEE ZULUMAATIL ARD\nPeace be upon you, O light of Allah in the darkness of the earth.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عِمَادَ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA I'MAADAD DEEN\nPeace be upon you, O pillar of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اٰدَمَ صَفِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA AADAMA SAFIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Adam, the chosen one of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ نُوْحٍ نَجِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA NOOHIN NAJIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Nuh, the confidant of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Ibrahim, the intimate friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اِسْمَاعِيْلَ ذَبِيْحِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA ISMAA'EELA DHABEEHILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Isma’il, the one offered in sacrifice to Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MOOSAA KALEEMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Musa, who spoke with Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA I'EESAA ROOHILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Isa, the spirit of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدٍ حَبِيْبِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MUHAMMADIN HABEEBILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Muhammad, the beloved of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَلِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WALIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Amir al-Mu’minin, the friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA SAYYIDATI NISAA'IL A'ALAMEENA FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'\nPeace be upon you, O heir of the mistress of the women of the worlds, Fatimah al-Zahra.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHAL HASANI WAL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon you, O heir of al-Hasan and al-Husayn.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ زَيْنِ الْعَابِدِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYNI ZAYNIL A'ABIDEEN\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Ali son of al-Husayn, Zayn al-Abidin.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ بَاقِرِ عِلْمِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MUHAMMADIBNI A'LIYYIN BAAQIRI I'LMIL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Muhammad son of Ali, who laid open the knowledge of the first and the last.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ الصَّادِقِ الْبَاۤرِّ الْاَمِيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA JA'FARIBNI MUHAMMADINIS SAADIQIL BAARRIL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Ja’far son of Muhammad, the truthful, the righteous, the trustworthy.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مُوْسَى بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ الْكَاظِمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MOOSABNI JA'FARINIL KAAZIM\nPeace be upon you, O heir of Musa son of Ja’far, al-Kazim.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ الشَّهِيْدُ الْغَرِيْبُ الْمَسْمُوْمُ الْمَقْتُوْلُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIDDEEQUSH SHAHEEDUL GHAREEBUL MASMOOMUL MAQTOOL\nPeace be upon you, O truthful one, martyr, stranger, poisoned and slain.\nاَشْهَدُ بِاللّٰهِ اَنَّكَ اَقَمْتَ الصَّلَاةَ وَاٰتَيْتَ الزَّكَاةَ\nASH-HADU BILLAAHI ANNAKA AQAMTAS SALAATA WA AATAYTAZ ZAKAAH\nI bear witness by Allah that you established the prayer and gave the zakat,\nوَاَمَرْتَ بِالْمَعْرُوْفِ وَنَهَيْتَ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ\nWA AMARTA BIL MA'ROOFI WA NAHAYTA A'NIL MUNKAR\nenjoined what is right and forbade what is wrong,\nوَعَبَدْتَ اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصًا حَتّٰۤى اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nWA A'BADTALLAAHA MUKHLISAN HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nand worshipped Allah sincerely until certainty came to you.\nقَتَلَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ بِالْاَيْدِيْ وَالْاَلْسُنِ\nQATALALLAAHU MAN QATALAKA BIL AYDEE WAL ALSUN\nMay Allah slay those who killed you, with their hands and with their tongues.\nعَلَيْكَ سَلَامُ اللّٰهِ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nA'LAYKA SALAAMULLAAHI YAA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nUpon you be the peace of Allah, O my master, and His mercy and blessings.\nThen kiss the tomb, lay your right cheek on it and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِلَيْكَ صَمَدْتُ مِنْ اَرْضِيْ وَقَطَعْتُ الْبِلَادَ رَجَاۤءَ رَحْمَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA ILAYKA SAMADTU MIN ARDEE WA QATA'TUL BILAADA RAJAA'A RAHMATIK\nO Allah, to You I have made my way from my land, crossing countries in hope of Your mercy;\nفَلَا تُخَيِّبْنِيْ وَلَا تَرُدَّنِيْ بِغَيْرِ قَضَاۤءِ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ\nFALAA TUKHAYYIBNEE WA LAA TARUDDANEE BIGHAYRI QADAA'I HAWAA'IJEE\nso do not disappoint me, and do not send me back without my needs fulfilled.\nوَارْحَمْ تَقَلُّبِيْ عَلٰى قَبْرِ ابْنِ اَخِيْ رَسُوْلِكَ صَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWARHAM TAQALLUBEE A'LAA QABRIBNI AKHEE RASOOLIKA SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nHave mercy on my turning about on the tomb of the son of Your Messenger’s brother, Your blessings be upon him and his family.\nبِاَبِيْ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE\nMay my father and mother be your ransom!\nاَتَيْتُكَ زَاۤئِرًا وَافِدًا عَاۤئِذًا مِمَّا جَنَيْتُ عَلٰى نَفْسِيْ وَاحْتَطَبْتُ عَلٰى ظَهْرِيْ\nATAYTUKA ZAA'IRAN WAAFIDAN A'A'IDHAN MIMMAA JANAYTU A'LAA NAFSEE WAHTATABTU A'LAA ZAHREE\nI have come to you as a visitor and a guest, seeking refuge from the wrong I have done myself and the burden I have loaded on my back.\nفَكُنْ لِيْ شَافِعًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَعَالٰى يَوْمَ فَقْرِيْ وَفَاقَتِيْ\nFAKUN LEE SHAAFI'AN ILALLAAHI TA'AALAA YAWMA FAQREE WA FAAQATEE\nSo be my intercessor with Allah, the Exalted, on the day of my poverty and need,\nفَاِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ مَقَامًا مَحْمُوْدًا وَجَاهًا وَجِيْهًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nFA-INNA LAKA I'NDALLAAHI MAQAAMAN MAHMOODAN WA JAAHAN WAJEEHAN FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nfor you have a praised station with Allah and an honoured standing in this world and the hereafter.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE AJMA'EEN\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and all his family.\nThen lay your left cheek on the tomb and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَيْكَ بِحُبِّهِمْ وَاَتَوَسَّلُ اِلَيْكَ بِوِلَايَتِهِمْ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAQARRABU ILAYKA BIHUBBIHIM WA ATAWASSALU ILAYKA BIWILAAYATIHIM\nO Allah, I seek nearness to You through love of them and seek a means to You through loyalty to them.\nوَاَتَوَلّٰۤى اٰخِرَهُمْ بِمَا تَوَلَّيْتُ بِهٖۤ اَوَّلَهُمْ\nWA ATAWALLAA AAKHIRAHUM BIMAA TAWALLAYTU BIHEE AWWALAHUM\nI am loyal to the last of them as I was loyal to the first of them,\nوَاَبْرَاُ مِنْ كُلِّ وَلِيْجَةٍ دُوْنَهُمْ\nWA ABRA'U MIN KULLI WALEEJATIN DOONAHUM\nand I disown every intimate taken in place of them.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنِ الَّذِيْنَ بَدَّلُوْا نِعْمَتَكَ وَاتَّهَمُوْا نَبِيَّكَ\nALLAAHUMMAL A'NIL LADHEENA BADDALOO NI'MATAKA WATTAHAMOO NABIYYAK\nO Allah, curse those who exchanged Your blessing, cast suspicion on Your Prophet,\nوَجَحَدُوْا بِاٰيَاتِكَ وَسَخِرُوْا بِاِمَامِكَ\nWA JAHADOO BI-AAYAATIKA WA SAKHIROO BI-IMAAMIK\ndenied Your signs, mocked Your Imam,\nوَحَمَلُوا النَّاسَ عَلٰۤى اَكْتَافِ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nWA HAMALUN NAASA A'LAA AKTAAFI AALI MUHAMMAD\nand set the people upon the shoulders of the family of Muhammad.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ اَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَيْكَ بِاللَّعْنَةِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَالْبَرَاۤءَةِ مِنْهُمْ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ATAQARRABU ILAYKA BIL LA'NATI A'LAYHIM WAL BARAA'ATI MINHUM FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nO Allah, I seek nearness to You by cursing them and disowning them in this world and the hereafter,\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen go to the side of the feet and recite:\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA YABNA RASOOLILLAAH\nMay Allah bless you, O son of the Messenger of Allah.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا الْحَسَنِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA YAA ABAL HASAN\nMay Allah bless you, O Abu al-Hasan.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى رُوْحِكَ الطَّيِّبِ وَبَدَنِكَ الزَّكِيِّ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAA ROOHIKAT TAYYIBI WA BADANIKAZ ZAKIYY\nMay Allah bless your good soul and your pure body.\nصَبَرْتَ وَاحْتَسَبْتَ وَاَنْتَ الصَّادِقُ الْمُصَدِّقُ\nSABARTA WAHTASABTA WA ANTAS SAADIQUL MUSADDIQ\nYou were patient and sought your reward from Allah; you are the truthful, who confirmed the truth.\nقَتَلَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ قَتَلَكَ وَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ مَنْ ظَلَمَكَ بِالْاَيْدِيْ وَالْاَلْسُنِ\nQATALALLAAHU MAN QATALAKA WA LA'ANALLAAHU MAN ZALAMAKA BIL AYDEE WAL ALSUN\nMay Allah slay those who killed you, and may Allah curse those who wronged you with their hands and their tongues.\nعَلَيْكَ سَلَامُ اللّٰهِ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَابْنَ مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nA'LAYKA SALAAMULLAAHI YAA MAWLAAYA WABNA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nUpon you be the peace of Allah, O my master and son of my master, and His mercy and blessings.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ اِمَامُ الْهُدٰى وَالْوَلِيُّ الْمُرْشِدُ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA IMAAMUL HUDAA WAL WALIYYUL MURSHID\nI bear witness that you are the Imam of guidance and the friend who guides aright.\nاَبْرَاُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكَ وَاَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِمُوَالَاتِكَ\nABRA'U ILALLAAHI MIN A'DAA'IKA WA ATAQARRABU ILALLAAHI BIMUWAALAATIK\nBefore Allah I disown your enemies, and I seek nearness to Allah through loyalty to you.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nMay Allah bless you, and His mercy and blessings be upon you.\nThen stand behind the head, face Karbala and recite this ziyarat of Imam Husayn (a.s.):\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Abu Abdillah,\nوَعَلَى الْاَرْوَاحِ الَّتِيْ حَلَّتْ بِفِنَاۤئِكَ وَاَنَاخَتْ بِرَحْلِكَ\nWA A'LAL ARWAAHIL LATEE HALLAT BIFINAA'IKA WA ANAAKHAT BIRAHLIK\nand upon the souls that alighted in your courtyard and halted with you.\nعَلَيْكَ مِنِّيْ سَلَامُ اللّٰهِ اَبَدًا مَا بَقِيْتُ وَبَقِيَ اللَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ\nA'LAYKA MINNEE SALAAMULLAAHI ABADAN MAA BAQEETU WA BAQIYAL LAYLU WAN NAHAAR\nUpon you be the peace of Allah from me forever, as long as I remain and night and day remain.\nوَلَا جَعَلَهُ اللّٰهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنْ زِيَارَتِكُمْ\nWA LAA JA'ALAHULLAAHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MIN ZIYAARATIKUM\nMay Allah not make this my last visit to you.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ وَعَلٰى عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI WA A'LAA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYN\nPeace be upon al-Hasan and al-Husayn, upon Ali son of al-Husayn,\nوَعَلٰۤى اَوْلَادِ الْحُسَيْنِ وَعَلٰۤى اَصْحَابِ الْحُسَيْنِ\nWA A'LAA AWLAADIL HUSAYNI WA A'LAA AS-HAABIL HUSAYN\nupon the children of al-Husayn and upon the companions of al-Husayn.\nوَلَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى قَاتِلِ الْحُسَيْنِ\nWA LA'NATULLAAHI A'LAA QAATILIL HUSAYN\nThe curse of Allah be upon the killer of al-Husayn.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْ اَوَّلَ ظَالِمٍ ظَلَمَ حَقَّ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰخِرَ تَابِعٍ لَهٗ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ\nALLAAHUMMAL A'N AWWALA ZAALIMIN ZALAMA HAQQA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WA AAKHIRA TAABI'IN LAHOO A'LAA DHAALIK\nO Allah, curse the first oppressor who usurped the right of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and the last who followed him in that.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنِ الْعِصَابَةَ الَّتِيْ جَاهَدَتِ الْحُسَيْنَ وَشَايَعَتْ وَبَايَعَتْ وَتَابَعَتْ عَلٰى قَتْلِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMAL A'NIL I'SAABATAL LATEE JAAHADATIL HUSAYNA WA SHAAYA'AT WA BAAYA'AT WA TAABA'AT A'LAA QATLIH\nO Allah, curse the band that fought al-Husayn, and those who sided, pledged and joined together in killing him.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ الْعَنْهُمْ جَمِيْعًا\nALLAAHUMMAL A'NHUM JAMEE'AA\nO Allah, curse them all.\nThen return to the head and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَابْنَ مَوْلَايَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA WABNA MAWLAAYA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O my master and son of my master, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ تَشْهَدُ مَقَامِيْ وَتَسْمَعُ كَلَامِيْ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA TASH-HADU MAQAAMEE WA TASMA'U KALAAMEE\nI bear witness that you see where I stand and hear my words,\nوَاَنْتَ حَيٌّ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ مَرْزُوْقٌ\nWA ANTA HAYYUN I'NDA RABBIKA MARZOOQ\nand that you are alive with your Lord, receiving sustenance.\nوَنَسْاَلُ اللّٰهَ رَبِّيْ وَرَبَّكُمْ قَضَاۤءَ حَوَاۤئِجِيْ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWA NAS'ALULLAAHA RABBEE WA RABBAKUM QADAA'A HAWAA'IJEE FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nWe ask Allah, my Lord and yours, to fulfil my needs in this world and the hereafter,\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen move forward and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الشَّهِيْدُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHASH SHAHEED\nPeace be upon you, O martyr.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْاِمَامُ الْمَعْصُوْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL IMAAMUL MA'SOOM\nPeace be upon you, O sinless Imam.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْاِمَامُ الْمَظْلُوْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL IMAAMUL MAZLOOM\nPeace be upon you, O wronged Imam.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْاِمَامُ الْمَسْمُوْمُ الْمَغْمُوْمُ الْمَهْمُوْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL IMAAMUL MASMOOMUL MAGHMOOMUL MAHMOOM\nPeace be upon you, O Imam who was poisoned, grieved and sorrowful.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ الْاِمَامُ الْهَادِيْ وَالْوَلِيُّ الْمُرْشِدُ\nASH-HADU ANNAKAL IMAAMUL HAADEE WAL WALIYYUL MURSHID\nI bear witness that you are the guiding Imam and the friend who guides aright.\nاَبْرَاُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكَ وَاَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِمُوَالَاتِكَ\nABRA'U ILALLAAHI MIN A'DAA'IKA WA ATAQARRABU ILALLAAHI BIMUWAALAATIK\nBefore Allah I disown your enemies, and I seek nearness to Allah through loyalty to you.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰۤى اٰبَاۤئِكَ وَاَوْلَادِكَ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA AABAA'IKA WA AWLAADIK\nMay Allah bless you, your forefathers and your children,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nby Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nThen go to the head and pray the two-unit prayer of ziyarat: in the first unit, after [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), recite [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) up to fifty times; in the second, after al-Fatihah, any surah.\nAfter the prayer, glorify Allah and ask forgiveness for yourself, your parents, your friends and all believing men and women. Then, in prostration, recite the dua said after the prayer of ziyarat, which opens «اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ صَلَّيْتُ وَرَكَعْتُ».",
    "Ziyarat of the Seven Hadith\nAfter the ghusl of ziyarat, stand before the tomb with your back to the qiblah, make the intention of the ziyarat and recite:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ عَلِيًّا وَلِيُّهٗ وَوَصِيُّ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA A'LIYYAN WALIYYUHOO WA WASIYYU RASOOLIH\nand I bear witness that Ali is His friend and the successor of His Messenger.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مَلَاۤئِكَتِكَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MALAA'IKATIKAL MUQARRABEEN\nO Allah, bless Your angels who are brought near.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ وَالْمُرْسَلِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL ANBIYAA'I WAL MURSALEEN\nO Allah, bless the prophets and the messengers.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَى الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAL A'IMMATIL MA'SOOMEEN\nO Allah, bless the sinless Imams.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مَوْلَانَا وَمُقْتَدَانَا\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MAWLAANAA WA MUQTADAANAA\nO Allah, bless our master and the one we follow,\nاِمَامِ الْهُدٰى وَالْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقٰى وَحُجَّتِكَ عَلٰۤى اَهْلِ الدُّنْيَا\nIMAAMIL HUDAA WAL U'RWATIL WUTHQAA WA HUJJATIKA A'LAA AHLID DUNYAA\nthe Imam of guidance, the firmest handle and Your proof over the people of the world,\nاَلَّذِيْ قَالَ فِيْ حَقِّهٖ سَيِّدُ الْوَرٰى وَسَنَدُ الْبَرَايَا\nALLADHEE QAALA FEE HAQQIHEE SAYYIDUL WARAA WA SANADUL BARAAYAA\nof whom the master of all creatures and the support of mankind said:\nسَتُدْفَنُ بَضْعَةٌ مِنِّيْ بِاَرْضِ خُرَاسَانَ\nSATUDFANU BAD'ATUN MINNEE BI-ARDI KHURAASAAN\n“A part of me will be buried in the land of Khurasan.\nمَا زَارَهَا مَكْرُوْبٌ اِلَّا نَفَّسَ اللّٰهُ كَرْبَهٗ\nMAA ZAARAHAA MAKROOBUN ILLAA NAFFASALLAAHU KARBAH\nNo one in distress visits it but that Allah relieves his distress,\nوَلَا مُذْنِبٌ اِلَّا غَفَرَ ذَنْبَهٗ\nWA LAA MUDHNIBUN ILLAA GHAFARA DHANBAH\nand no sinner but that He forgives his sin.”\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بِشَفَاعَتِهِ الْمَقْبُوْلَةِ وَدَرَجَتِهِ الرَّفِيْعَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA BISHAFAA'ATIHIL MAQBOOLATI WA DARAJATIHIR RAFEE'AH\nO Allah, by his accepted intercession and his lofty rank,\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُنَفِّسَ بِهٖ كَرْبِيْ وَتَغْفِرَ بِهٖ ذَنْبِيْ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUNAFFISA BIHEE KARBEE WA TAGHFIRA BIHEE DHANBEE\nI ask You to relieve my distress through him and forgive my sin through him,\nوَتُسْمِعَهٗ كَلَامِيْ وَتُبَلِّغَهٗ سَلَامِيْ\nWA TUSMI'AHOO KALAAMEE WA TUBALLIGHAHOO SALAAMEE\nto let him hear my words and to convey my greeting to him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O proof of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا نُوْرَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA NOORALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O light of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَيْبَةَ عِلْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'YBATA I'LMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O keeper of Allah’s knowledge.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَعْدِنَ حِكْمَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MA'DINA HIKMATILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O mine of Allah’s wisdom.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَامِلَ كِتَابِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HAAMILA KITAABILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O bearer of the Book of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَافِظَ سِرِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HAAFIZA SIRRILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O guardian of Allah’s secret.\nاَنْتَ الَّذِيْ قَالَ فِيْكَ قَاتِلُ الْكَفَرَةِ وَقَامِعُ الْفَجَرَةِ\nANTAL LADHEE QAALA FEEKA QAATILUL KAFARATI WA QAAMI'UL FAJARAH\nYou are the one of whom the slayer of the unbelievers and subduer of the wicked,\nعَلِيٌّ اَمِيْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَوَصِيُّ رَسُوْلِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nA'LIYYUN AMEERUL MU'MINEENA WA WASIYYU RASOOLI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nAli, Amir al-Mu’minin and successor of the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds,\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ وَسَلَامُهٗ عَلَيْهِ\nSALAWAATULLAAHI WA SALAAMUHOO A'LAYH\nAllah’s blessings and peace be upon him, said:\nسَيُقْتَلُ رَجُلٌ مِنْ وُلْدِيْ بِاَرْضِ خُرَاسَانَ بِالسَّمِّ ظُلْمًا\nSAYUQTALU RAJULUN MIN WULDEE BI-ARDI KHURAASAANA BIS SAMMI ZULMAA\n“A man among my descendants will be killed unjustly by poison in the land of Khurasan.\nاِسْمُهٗ اِسْمِيْ وَاسْمُ اَبِيْهِ اسْمُ ابْنِ عِمْرَانَ مُوْسٰى عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ\nISMUHOO ISMEE WASMU ABEEHISMUBNI I'MRAANA MOOSAA A'LAYHIS SALAAM\nHis name is my name, and his father’s name is the name of the son of Imran, Musa, peace be upon him.\nاَلَا فَمَنْ زَارَهٗ فِيْ غُرْبَتِهٖ غَفَرَ اللّٰهُ لَهٗ ذُنُوْبَهٗ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْهَا وَمَا تَاَخَّرَ\nALAA FAMAN ZAARAHOO FEE GHURBATIHEE GHAFARALLAAHU LAHOO DHUNOOBAHOO MAA TAQADDAMA MINHAA WA MAA TA'AKHKHAR\nWhoever visits him in his exile, Allah will forgive him his sins, the earlier and the later,\nوَلَوْ كَانَتْ مِثْلَ عَدَدِ النُّجُوْمِ وَقَطْرِ الْاَمْطَارِ وَوَرَقِ الْاَشْجَارِ\nWA LAW KAANAT MITHLA A'DADIN NUJOOMI WA QATRIL AMTAARI WA WARAQIL ASHJAAR\neven if they were as many as the stars, the drops of rain and the leaves of the trees.”\nمَوْلَايَ مَوْلَايَ هَاۤ اَنَا ذَا وَاقِفٌ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nMAWLAAYA MAWLAAYA HAA ANAA DHAA WAAQIFUN BAYNA YADAYK\nMy master, my master, here I am standing before you,\nوَذُنُوْبِيْ مِثْلُ عَدَدِ النُّجُوْمِ وَقَطْرِ الْاَمْطَارِ وَوَرَقِ الْاَشْجَارِ\nWA DHUNOOBEE MITHLU A'DADIN NUJOOMI WA QATRIL AMTAARI WA WARAQIL ASHJAAR\nand my sins are as many as the stars, the drops of rain and the leaves of the trees,\nوَلَيْسَ لِيْ وَسِيْلَةٌ اِلٰى مَحْوِهَاۤ اِلَّا رِضَاكَ\nWA LAYSA LEE WASEELATUN ILAA MAHWIHAA ILLAA RIDAAK\nand I have no means of wiping them out but your good pleasure.\nمَوْلَايَ مَاۤ اَحْسِبُ فِيْ صَحِيْفَتِيْ عَمَلًا اَرْجٰى عِنْدِيْ مِنْ زِيَارَتِكَ\nMAWLAAYA MAA AHSIBU FEE SAHEEFATEE A'MALAN ARJAA I'NDEE MIN ZIYAARATIK\nMy master, I count no deed in my record more hopeful for me than my visit to you.\nكَيْفَ وَقَدْ قَالَ فِيْ حَقِّهَا بَاقِرُ عِلْمِ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ وَالْاٰخِرِيْنَ صَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْهِ\nKAYFA WA QAD QAALA FEE HAQQIHAA BAAQIRU I'LMIL AWWALEENA WAL AAKHIREENA SALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYH\nHow could it be otherwise, when the one who laid open the knowledge of the first and the last, Allah’s blessings be upon him, said of it:\nيَخْرُجُ رَجُلٌ مِنْ وُلْدِيْ اِسْمُهٗ اِسْمُ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nYAKHRUJU RAJULUN MIN WULDEE ISMUHOO ISMU AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\n“A man among my descendants will come forth whose name is the name of Amir al-Mu’minin,\nفَيُدْفَنُ بِاَرْضِ خُرَاسَانَ\nFAYUDFANU BI-ARDI KHURAASAAN\nand he will be buried in the land of Khurasan.\nمَنْ زَارَهٗ عَارِفًا بِحَقِّهٖ اَعْطَاهُ اللّٰهُ اَجْرَ مَنْ اَنْفَقَ مِنْ قَبْلِ الْفَتْحِ وَقَاتَلَ\nMAN ZAARAHOO A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIHEE A'TAAHULLAAHU AJRA MAN ANFAQA MIN QABLIL FAT-HI WA QAATAL\nWhoever visits him knowing his right, Allah will give him the reward of one who spent and fought before the victory.”\nفَاَتَيْتُكَ زَاۤئِرًا لَكَ عَارِفًا بِحَقِّكَ\nFA-ATAYTUKA ZAA'IRAN LAKA A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIK\nSo I have come to you, visiting you and knowing your right,\nعَالِمًا بِاَنَّكَ اِمَامٌ مُفْتَرَضُ الطَّاعَةِ غَرِيْبٌ شَهِيْدٌ\nA'ALIMAN BI-ANNAKA IMAAMUN MUFTARADUT TAA'ATI GHAREEBUN SHAHEED\nknowing that you are an Imam whom it is obligatory to obey, a stranger and a martyr,\nرَاجِيًا بِمَا قَالَهُ الصَّادِقُ عَلَيْهِ الصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ\nRAAJIYAN BIMAA QAALAHUS SAADIQU A'LAYHIS SALAATU WAS SALAAM\nhoping for what al-Sadiq, blessings and peace be upon him, said:\nيُقْتَلُ حَفَدَتِيْ بِاَرْضِ خُرَاسَانَ فِيْ مَدِيْنَةٍ يُقَالُ لَهَا طُوْسُ\nYUQTALU HAFADATEE BI-ARDI KHURAASAANA FEE MADEENATIN YUQAALU LAHAA TOOS\n“My grandson will be killed in the land of Khurasan, in a city called Tus.\nمَنْ زَارَهٗ عَارِفًا بِحَقِّهٖ اَخَذْتُهٗ بِيَدِيْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَاَدْخَلْتُهُ الْجَنَّةَ\nMAN ZAARAHOO A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIHEE AKHADHTUHOO BIYADEE YAWMAL QIYAAMATI WA ADKHALTUHUL JANNAH\nWhoever visits him knowing his right, I will take him by the hand on the Day of Resurrection and bring him into Paradise,\nوَاِنْ كَانَ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْكَبَاۤئِرِ\nWA IN KAANA MIN AHLIL KABAA'IR\neven if he was one who committed major sins.”\nقِيْلَ لَهٗ مَا عِرْفَانُ حَقِّهٖ\nQEELA LAHOO MAA I'RFAANU HAQQIH\nHe was asked, “What is knowing his right?”\nقَالَ اَلْعِلْمُ بِاَنَّهٗ مُفْتَرَضُ الطَّاعَةِ غَرِيْبٌ شَهِيْدٌ\nQAALAL I'LMU BI-ANNAHOO MUFTARADUT TAA'ATI GHAREEBUN SHAHEED\nHe said, “To know that he is one whom it is obligatory to obey, a stranger and a martyr.\nمَنْ زَارَهٗ عَارِفًا بِحَقِّهٖ اَعْطَاهُ اللّٰهُ اَجْرَ سَبْعِيْنَ شَهِيْدًا\nMAN ZAARAHOO A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIHEE A'TAAHULLAAHU AJRA SAB'EENA SHAHEEDAA\nWhoever visits him knowing his right, Allah will give him the reward of seventy martyrs\nمِمَّنِ اسْتُشْهِدَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nMIMMANIS TUSH-HIDA BAYNA YADAY RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nof those martyred before the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and his family.”\nيَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nYABNA RASOOLILLAAH\nO son of the Messenger of Allah,\nاَبْتَغِيْ بِزِيَارَتِكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ تَعَالٰى غُفْرَانَ ذُنُوْبِيْ وَذُنُوْبِ وَالِدَيَّ وَالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ\nABTAGHEE BIZIYAARATIKA MINALLAAHI TA'AALAA GHUFRAANA DHUNOOBEE WA DHUNOOBI WAALIDAYYA WAL MU'MINEENA WAL MU'MINAAT\nby visiting you I seek from Allah, the Exalted, forgiveness of my sins and the sins of my parents and of the believing men and women,\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ الْاِتْيَانَ الْمَوْعُوْدَ فِي الْمَوَاطِنِ الثَّلَاثِ\nWA AS'ALUKAL ITYAANAL MAW'OODA FIL MAWAATINITH THALAATH\nand I ask you for the coming you promised at the three places:\nعِنْدَ تَطَايُرِ الْكُتُبِ وَعِنْدَ الصِّرَاطِ وَعِنْدَ الْمِيْزَانِ\nI'NDA TATAAYURIL KUTUBI WA I'NDAS SIRAATI WA I'NDAL MEEZAAN\n“when the records fly, at the Bridge and at the Scales.”\nوَقُلْتَ وَقَوْلُكَ حَقٌّ\nWA QULTA WA QAWLUKA HAQQ\nAnd you said, and your word is true:\nاِنَّ شَرَّ مَا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ فِيْ زَمَانِيْ يَقْتُلُنِيْ بِالسَّمِّ\nINNA SHARRA MAA KHALAQALLAAHU FEE ZAMAANEE YAQTULUNEE BIS SAMM\n“The worst of what Allah has created in my time will kill me with poison,\nثُمَّ يَدْفِنُنِيْ فِيْ دَارِ مَضْيَعَةٍ وَبِلَادِ غُرْبَةٍ\nTHUMMA YADFINUNEE FEE DAARI MADYA'ATIN WA BILAADI GHURBAH\nthen bury me in a forsaken place, in a land of exile.\nاَلَا فَمَنْ زَارَنِيْ فِيْ غُرْبَتِيْ كَتَبَ اللّٰهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ لَهٗ اَجْرَ مِائَةِ اَلْفِ حَاۤجٍّ وَمُعْتَمِرٍ وَمِائَةِ اَلْفِ مُجَاهِدٍ\nALAA FAMAN ZAARANEE FEE GHURBATEE KATABALLAAHU A'ZZA WA JALLA LAHOO AJRA MI'ATI ALFI HAAJJIN WA MU'TAMIRIN WA MI'ATI ALFI MUJAAHID\nWhoever visits me in my exile, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will write for him the reward of a hundred thousand pilgrims of hajj and umrah and a hundred thousand fighters in His way,\nوَحُشِرَ فِيْ زُمْرَتِنَا وَجُعِلَ فِي الدَّرَجَاتِ الْعُلٰى مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ رَفِيْقًا\nWA HUSHIRA FEE ZUMRATINAA WA JU'ILA FID DARAJAATIL U'LAA MINAL JANNATI RAFEEQAA\nand he will be gathered in our company and made a companion in the highest ranks of Paradise.”\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِيْ وَفَّقَنِيْ لِزِيَارَتِكَ فِي الْبُقْعَةِ الَّتِيْ قُلْتَ فِيْ حَقِّهَا\nAL-HAMDU LILLAAHIL LADHEE WAFFAQANEE LIZIYAARATIKA FIL BUQ'ATIL LATEE QULTA FEE HAQQIHAA\nPraise be to Allah, who granted me to visit you in the spot of which you said:\nهِيَ وَاللّٰهِ رَوْضَةٌ مِنْ رِيَاضِ الْجَنَّةِ\nHIYA WALLAAHI RAWDATUN MIN RIYAADIL JANNAH\n“By Allah, it is a garden of the gardens of Paradise.\nمَنْ زَارَنِيْ فِيْ تِلْكَ الْبُقْعَةِ كَانَ كَمَنْ زَارَ رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nMAN ZAARANEE FEE TILKAL BUQ'ATI KAANA KAMAN ZAARA RASOOLALLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nWhoever visits me in that spot is like one who has visited the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and his family,\nوَكَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَهٗ ثَوَابَ اَلْفِ حَجَّةٍ مَبْرُوْرَةٍ وَاَلْفِ عُمْرَةٍ مَقْبُوْلَةٍ\nWA KATABALLAAHU LAHOO THAWAABA ALFI HAJJATIN MABROORATIN WA ALFI U'MRATIN MAQBOOLAH\nand Allah will write for him the reward of a thousand accepted hajj and a thousand accepted umrah,\nوَكُنْتُ اَنَا وَاٰبَاۤئِيْ شُفَعَاۤءَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ\nWA KUNTU ANAA WA AABAA'EE SHUFA'AA'AHOO YAWMAL QIYAAMAH\nand I and my forefathers will be his intercessors on the Day of Resurrection.”\nفَكُنْ شَفِيْعِيْ بِاٰبَاۤئِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ وَاَوْلَادِكَ الْمُنْتَجَبِيْنَ\nFAKUN SHAFEE'EE BI-AABAA'IKAT TAAHIREENA WA AWLAADIKAL MUNTAJABEEN\nSo be my intercessor, with your pure forefathers and your chosen children.\nمَوْلَايَ اَنْتَ الَّذِيْ لَا يَزُوْرُكَ اِلَّا الْخَوَاۤصُّ مِنَ الشِّيْعَةِ\nMAWLAAYA ANTAL LADHEE LAA YAZOORUKA ILLAL KHAWAASSU MINASH SHEE'AH\nMy master, you are the one whom only the elect among the Shia visit.\nفَبِحَقِّكَ وَبِحَقِّ شِيْعَتِكَ اَنْ تُشَفِّعَنِيْ\nFABIHAQQIKA WA BIHAQQI SHEE'ATIKA AN TUSHAFFI'ANEE\nSo by your right and the right of your Shia, grant me your intercession,\nوَتَسْاَلَ اللّٰهَ اَنْ يَحْشُرَنِيْ مَعَ شِيْعَتِكَ فِيْ مُسْتَقَرٍّ مِنَ الرَّحْمَةِ مَعَكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ\nWA TAS'ALALLAAHA AN YAHSHURANEE MA'A SHEE'ATIKA FEE MUSTAQARRIN MINAR RAHMATI MA'AKUM AHLAL BAYT\nand ask Allah to gather me with your Shia in an abode of mercy, with you, O Ahl al-Bayt.\nمَعَكُمْ مَعَكُمْ لَا مَعَ غَيْرِكُمْ\nMA'AKUM MA'AKUM LAA MA'A GHAYRIKUM\nWith you, with you, not with any other than you!\nبَرِئْتُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكُمْ وَتَقَرَّبْتُ بِاللّٰهِ اِلَيْكُمْ\nBARI'TU ILALLAAHI MIN A'DAA'IKUM WA TAQARRABTU BILLAAHI ILAYKUM\nBefore Allah I have disowned your enemies, and by Allah I have drawn near to you.\nاِنِّيْ مُؤْمِنٌ بِاِيَابِكُمْ مُنْتَظِرٌ لِاَمْرِكُمْ\nINNEE MU'MINUN BI-IYAABIKUM MUNTAZIRUN LI-AMRIKUM\nI believe in your return and await your cause;\nمُصَدِّقٌ بِرَجْعَتِكُمْ مُتَرَقِّبٌ لِدَوْلَتِكُمْ\nMUSADDIQUN BIRAJ'ATIKUM MUTARAQQIBUN LIDAWLATIKUM\nI affirm your coming back and watch for your rule;\nعَارِفٌ بِعِظَمِ شَاْنِكُمْ عَالِمٌ بِضَلَالَةِ مَنْ خَالَفَكُمْ\nA'ARIFUN BI-I'ZAMI SHA'NIKUM A'ALIMUN BIDALAALATI MAN KHAALAFAKUM\nI know the greatness of your standing and the error of those who oppose you;\nمُوَالٍ لَكُمْ وَلِاَوْلِيَاۤئِكُمْ مُبْغِضٌ لِاَعْدَاۤئِكُمْ\nMUWAALIN LAKUM WA LI-AWLIYAA'IKUM MUBGHIDUN LI-A'DAA'IKUM\nI am loyal to you and to your friends and hate your enemies;\nعَاۤئِذٌ لَاۤئِذٌ بِقُبُوْرِكُمْ\nA'A'IDHUN LAA'IDHUN BIQUBOORIKUM\nI seek refuge and shelter at your graves.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ النَّبِيِّ وَالْوَصِيِّ وَالْبَتُوْلِ وَالسِّبْطَيْنِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADININ NABIYYI WAL WASIYYI WAL BATOOLI WAS SIBTAYN\nO Allah, bless Muhammad the Prophet, the Successor, the Pure Lady, the two grandsons,\nوَالسَّجَّادِ وَالْبَاقِرِ وَالصَّادِقِ وَالْكَاظِمِ وَالرِّضَا\nWAS SAJJAADI WAL BAAQIRI WAS SAADIQI WAL KAAZIMI WAR RIDAA\nal-Sajjad, al-Baqir, al-Sadiq, al-Kazim, al-Rida,\nوَالتَّقِيِّ وَالنَّقِيِّ وَالْعَسْكَرِيِّ وَالْمَهْدِيِّ صَاحِبِ الزَّمَانِ\nWAT TAQIYYI WAN NAQIYYI WAL A'SKARIYYI WAL MAHDIYYI SAAHIBIZ ZAMAAN\nal-Taqi, al-Naqi, al-Askari and al-Mahdi, the Master of the Age,\nصَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nSALAWAATUKA A'LAYHIM AJMA'EEN\nYour blessings be upon them all.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰۤؤُلَاۤءِ سَادَتُنَا وَقَادَتُنَا وَهُدَاتُنَا وَدُعَاتُنَا\nALLAAHUMMA HAA'ULAA'I SAADATUNAA WA QAADATUNAA WA HUDAATUNAA WA DU'AATUNAA\nO Allah, these are our masters, our leaders, our guides and those who call us to You.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَفِّقْنَا لِطَاعَتِهِمْ وَارْزُقْنَا شَفَاعَتَهُمْ\nALLAAHUMMA WAFFIQNAA LITAA'ATIHIM WARZUQNAA SHAFAA'ATAHUM\nO Allah, grant us success in obeying them, grant us their intercession,\nوَاحْشُرْنَا فِيْ زُمْرَتِهِمْ وَاجْعَلْنَا مِنْ خِيَارِ مَوَالِيْهِمْ\nWAHSHURNAA FEE ZUMRATIHIM WAJ'ALNAA MIN KHIYAARI MAWAALEEHIM\ngather us in their company and make us among the best of their followers,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nby Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAYYIBEENAL MA'SOOMEEN\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and his good and sinless family,\nوَالْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nand praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\nThen lay your right cheek and then your left on the tomb and recite the duas for each in the tab \"From Rawdat al-Adhkar\". Pray the two-unit prayer of ziyarat at the head and ask Allah for what you need.",
    "From Tuhfat al-Za'ir\nStand facing the zarih and recite:\nاَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADU AN LAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU WAHDAHOO LAA SHAREEKA LAH\nI bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُهٗ وَرَسُوْلُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNA MUHAMMADAN A'BDUHOO WA RASOOLUH\nand I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ اَمِيْنِ اللّٰهِ عَلٰى وَحْيِهٖ وَعَزَاۤئِمِ اَمْرِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA RASOOLILLAAHI AMEENILLAAHI A'LAA WAHYIHEE WA A'ZAA'IMI AMRIH\nPeace be upon the Messenger of Allah, Allah’s trustee over His revelation and His firm commands,\nاَلْخَاتِمِ لِمَا سَبَقَ وَالْفَاتِحِ لِمَا اسْتَقْبَلَ وَالْمُهَيْمِنِ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ كُلِّهٖ\nAL-KHAATIMI LIMAA SABAQA WAL FAATIHI LIMAS TAQBALA WAL MUHAYMINI A'LAA DHAALIKA KULLIH\nthe seal of what went before, the opener of what was to come, and the guardian over all of it,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَوْلَانَا اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَسَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ وَاَبِ الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MAWLAANAA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA SAYYIDIL WASIYYEENA WA ABIL A'IMMATIL MA'SOOMEEN\nPeace be upon our master Amir al-Mu’minin, master of the successors and father of the sinless Imams,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ سَيِّدَةِ النِّسَاۤءِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'I SAYYIDATIN NISAA'I WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon Fatimah al-Zahra, mistress of women, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْاَئِمَّةِ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ سَادَةِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ وَكُبَرَاۤءِ الصِّدِّيْقِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL A'IMMATIL MA'SOOMEENA SAADATIL MUTTAQEENA WA KUBARAA'IS SIDDEEQEEN\nPeace be upon the sinless Imams, masters of the God-fearing, the greatest of the truthful,\nوَاَعْلَامِ الْمُهْتَدِيْنَ وَاَنْوَارِ الْعَارِفِيْنَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA A'LAAMIL MUHTADEENA WA ANWAARIL A'ARIFEENA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nthe signs of the rightly guided and the lights of those who know, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مَوْلَانَا وَسَيِّدِنَا الْاِمَامِ الْمَعْصُوْمِ اَبِي الْحَسَنِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسَى الرِّضَا\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MAWLAANAA WA SAYYIDINAL IMAAMIL MA'SOOMI ABIL HASANI A'LIYYIBNI MOOSAR RIDAA\nPeace be upon our master and our chief, the sinless Imam Abu al-Hasan Ali son of Musa al-Rida,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA NABIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Seal of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA SAYYIDIL WASIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the master of the successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Amir al-Mu’minin.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اِمَامِ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA IMAAMIL MUTTAQEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the Imam of the God-fearing.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ قَاۤئِدِ الْغُرِّ الْمُحَجَّلِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA QAA'IDIL GHURRIL MUHAJJALEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the leader of those with shining faces, hands and feet.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ فَاطِمَةَ الزَّهْرَاۤءِ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA FAATIMATAZ ZAHRAA'I SAYYIDATI NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Fatimah al-Zahra, mistress of the women of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ خَدِيْجَةَ الْكُبْرٰى اُمِّ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA KHADEEJATAL KUBRAA UMMIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Khadijah al-Kubra, mother of the believers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَبِيْ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ الْحُسَيْنِ الشَّهِيْدِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA ABEE A'BDILLAAHIL HUSAYNISH SHAHEED\nPeace be upon you, O son of Abu Abdillah al-Husayn, the martyr.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ الْحُسَيْنِ زَيْنِ الْعَابِدِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA A'LIYYIBNIL HUSAYNI ZAYNIL A'ABIDEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Ali son of al-Husayn, Zayn al-Abidin.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَبِيْ جَعْفَرٍ مُحَمَّدٍ الْبَاقِرِ لِعُلُوْمِ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA ABEE JA'FARIN MUHAMMADINIL BAAQIRI LI-U'LOOMID DEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Abu Ja’far Muhammad, who laid open the sciences of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَبِيْ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ جَعْفَرٍ الصَّادِقِ الْاَمِيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA ABEE A'BDILLAAHI JA'FARINIS SAADIQIL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Abu Abdillah Ja’far, the truthful, the trustworthy.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ اَبِي الْحَسَنِ مُوْسَى الْكَاظِمِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA ABIL HASANI MOOSAL KAAZIMI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O son of Abu al-Hasan Musa al-Kazim, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYAA ALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَبِيْبَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HABEEBALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O beloved of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفْوَةَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFWATALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O chosen one of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَمُوْدَ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'MOODAD DEEN\nPeace be upon you, O pillar of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَصِيَّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WASIYYA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O successor of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O proof of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَاۤصَّةَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAASSATALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O elect of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَالِصَةَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAALISATALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O purely devoted one of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْضِعَ سِرِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWDI'A SIRRILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O place of Allah’s secret.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَيْبَةَ عِلْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'YBATA I'LMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O keeper of Allah’s knowledge.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHAL ANBIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O heir of the prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَصِيَّ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WASIYYAL AWSIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O successor of the successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مِشْكَاةَ الضِّيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MISHKAATAD DIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O niche of radiance.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُنْتَهَى الْعُلْيَا\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUNTAHAL U'LYAA\nPeace be upon you, O summit of loftiness.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الشَّرَفِ الْاَثِيْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBASH SHARAFIL ATHEEL\nPeace be upon you, O you of deep-rooted honour.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ذَا الْفِعْلِ الْجَمِيْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA DHAL FI'LIL JAMEEL\nPeace be upon you, O you of beautiful deeds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الْاَصْلِ الْاَصِيْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBAL ASLIL ASEEL\nPeace be upon you, O you of noble origin.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اُسَّ الْاِيْمَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA USSAL EEMAAN\nPeace be upon you, O foundation of faith.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا شَرِيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SHAREEKAL QUR'AAN\nPeace be upon you, O companion of the Qur’an.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَعْدِنَ الْاِيْمَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MA'DINAL EEMAAN\nPeace be upon you, O mine of faith.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اِمَامَ الْاَبْرَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMAL ABRAAR\nPeace be upon you, O Imam of the righteous.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَصِيَّ الْمُخْتَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WASIYYAL MUKHTAAR\nPeace be upon you, O successor of the Chosen One.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُظْهِرَ الْاَسْرَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUZHIRAL ASRAAR\nPeace be upon you, O revealer of secrets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الْمُعْجِزَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBAL MU'JIZAAT\nPeace be upon you, O worker of miracles.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُوْضِحَ الْبَيِّنَاتِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MOODIHAL BAYYINAAT\nPeace be upon you, O you who made the clear proofs plain.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الصِّرَاطُ الْمُسْتَقِيْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIRAATUL MUSTAQEEM\nPeace be upon you, O straight path.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الدِّيْنُ الْقَوِيْمُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAD DEENUL QAWEEM\nPeace be upon you, O upright religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مِصْبَاحَ الْهُدٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MISBAAHAL HUDAA\nPeace be upon you, O lamp of guidance.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَاْوَى التُّقٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MA'WAT TUQAA\nPeace be upon you, O refuge of piety.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَجْدَ الْحِجٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAJDAL HIJAA\nPeace be upon you, O glory of understanding.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا طَوْدَ النُّهٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA TAWDAN NUHAA\nPeace be upon you, O mountain of reason.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الدَّاعِيْ اِلَى الْمَحَجَّةِ الْعُظْمٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAD DAA'EE ILAL MAHAJJATIL U'ZMAA\nPeace be upon you, O you who call to the greatest way,\nوَالظَّاعِنُ اِلَى الْغَايَةِ الْقُصْوٰى وَالسَّامِيْ اِلَى الْمَجْدِ وَالْعُلٰى\nWAZ ZAA'INU ILAL GHAAYATIL QUSWAA WAS SAAMEE ILAL MAJDI WAL U'LAA\nwho journey to the farthest goal and rise to glory and height.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْعَالِمُ بِالتَّاْوِيْلِ وَالذِّكْرٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL A'ALIMU BIT TA'WEELI WADH DHIKRAA\nPeace be upon you, O you who know the inner meaning and the reminder.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا دَلِيْلَ الرَّشَادِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA DALEELAR RASHAAD\nPeace be upon you, O guide to right conduct.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ السَّادَةِ الْاَمْجَادِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNAS SAADATIL AMJAAD\nPeace be upon you, O son of the glorious masters.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ الْقَادَةِ الزُّهَّادِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNAL QAADATIZ ZUHHAAD\nPeace be upon you, O son of the abstinent leaders.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مِصْبَاحَ الظُّلَمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MISBAAHAZ ZULAM\nPeace be upon you, O lamp in the darkness.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا يَنْبُوْعَ الْحِكَمِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA YANBOO'AL HIKAMI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you, O spring of wisdom, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَشْهَدُ يَا مَوْلَايَ اَنَّكَ الْمُطِيْعُ لِلّٰهِ الْقَاۤئِمُ بِاَمْرِ اللّٰهِ\nASH-HADU YAA MAWLAAYA ANNAKAL MUTEE'U LILLAAHIL QAA'IMU BI-AMRILLAAH\nI bear witness, O my master, that you are obedient to Allah, carrying out the command of Allah,\nاَلْعَامِلُ بِاِرَادَتِهِ الْفَاۤئِزُ بِكَرَامَتِهٖ\nAL-A'AMILU BI-IRAADATIHIL FAA'IZU BIKARAAMATIH\nacting by His will and winning His honour.\nاِصْطَفَاكَ اللّٰهُ لِعِلْمِهٖ وَاخْتَارَكَ لِسِرِّهٖ وَاَعَزَّكَ بِهُدَاهُ\nISTAFAAKALLAAHU LI-I'LMIHEE WAKHTAARAKA LISIRRIHEE WA A'AZZAKA BIHUDAAH\nAllah chose you for His knowledge, selected you for His secret, strengthened you with His guidance,\nوَخَصَّكَ بِبُرْهَانِهٖ وَاَيَّدَكَ بِرُوْحِهٖ\nWA KHASSAKA BIBURHAANIHEE WA AYYADAKA BIROOHIH\nsingled you out with His proof and supported you with His Spirit.\nوَرَضِيَكَ خَلِيْفَةً فِيْۤ اَرْضِهٖ وَدَاعِيًا اِلٰى حَقِّهٖ\nWA RADIYAKA KHALEEFATAN FEE ARDIHEE WA DAA'IYAN ILAA HAQQIH\nHe was pleased with you as His deputy in His earth, a caller to His truth,\nوَشَهِيْدًا عَلٰى خَلْقِهٖ وَنَاصِرًا لِدِيْنِهٖ وَحُجَّةً عَلٰى بَرِيَّتِهٖ\nWA SHAHEEDAN A'LAA KHALQIHEE WA NAASIRAN LIDEENIHEE WA HUJJATAN A'LAA BARIYYATIH\na witness over His creation, a helper of His religion, a proof over His creatures,\nوَتَرْجُمَانًا لِوَحْيِهٖ وَخَازِنًا لِعِلْمِهٖ وَمُسْتَوْدَعًا لِحِكْمَتِهٖ\nWA TARJUMAANAN LIWAHYIHEE WA KHAAZINAN LI-I'LMIHEE WA MUSTAWDA'AN LIHIKMATIH\nan interpreter of His revelation, a treasurer of His knowledge and a keeper of His wisdom.\nعَصَمَكَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ وَبَرَّاَكَ مِنَ الْعُيُوْبِ\nA'SAMAKALLAAHU MINADH DHUNOOBI WA BARRA'AKA MINAL U'YOOB\nAllah kept you from sins and made you free of faults.\nزُرْتُكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ عَارِفًا بِحَقِّكَ مُسْتَبْصِرًا بِشَاْنِكَ مُهْتَدِيًا بِهُدَاكَ\nZURTUKA YAA MAWLAAYA A'ARIFAN BIHAQQIKA MUSTABSIRAN BISHA'NIKA MUHTADIYAN BIHUDAAK\nI have visited you, O my master, knowing your right, aware of your standing, guided by your guidance,\nمُقْتَفِيًا لِاَثَرِكَ مُتَّبِعًا لِسُنَّتِكَ مُتَمَسِّكًا بِحَبْلِكَ مُطِيْعًا لِاَمْرِكَ\nMUQTAFIYAN LI-ATHARIKA MUTTABI'AN LISUNNATIKA MUTAMASSIKAN BIHABLIKA MUTEE'AN LI-AMRIK\nfollowing your footsteps and your way, holding fast to your rope, obedient to your command,\nمُوَالِيًا لِوَلِيِّكَ مُعَادِيًا لِعَدُوِّكَ عَالِمًا بِاَنَّ الْحَقَّ لَكَ وَمَعَكَ\nMUWAALIYAN LIWALIYYIKA MU'AADIYAN LI-A'DUWWIKA A'ALIMAN BI-ANNAL HAQQA LAKA WA MA'AK\nloyal to your friend, hostile to your enemy, knowing that the truth is yours and with you,\nمُتَوَسِّلًا اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِكَ مُسْتَشْفِعًا اِلَيْهِ بِجَاهِكَ\nMUTAWASSILAN ILALLAAHI BIKA MUSTASHFI'AN ILAYHI BIJAAHIK\nseeking a means to Allah through you and seeking your intercession with Him by your standing.\nوَحَقٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَنْ لَا يُخَيِّبَ سَاۤئِلَهٗ وَالرَّاجِيَ مَا عِنْدَهٗ لِزَاۤئِرِكَ الْمُطِيْعِ لَكَ\nWA HAQQUN A'LAYHI AN LAA YUKHAYYIBA SAA'ILAHOO WAR RAAJIYA MAA I'NDAHOO LIZAA'IRIKAL MUTEE'I LAK\nIt is upon Him not to disappoint the one who asks of Him and hopes for what is with Him, for the sake of your visitor who obeys you.\nThen raise both hands and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَكَمَا وَفَّقْتَنِيْ لِلْاِيْمَانِ بِنَبِيِّكَ وَالتَّصْدِيْقِ بِكِتَابِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA FAKAMAA WAFFAQTANEE LIL EEMAANI BINABIYYIKA WAT TASDEEQI BIKITAABIK\nO Allah, as You have granted me faith in Your Prophet and belief in Your Book,\nوَمَنَنْتَ عَلَيَّ بِطَاعَتِهٖ وَاتِّبَاعِ مِلَّتِهٖ\nWA MANANTA A'LAYYA BITAA'ATIHEE WATTIBAA'I MILLATIH\nfavoured me with obedience to him and following his creed,\nوَهَدَيْتَنِيْۤ اِلٰى مَعْرِفَتِهٖ وَمَعْرِفَةِ الْاَئِمَّةِ مِنْ ذُرِّيَّتِهٖ\nWA HADAYTANEE ILAA MA'RIFATIHEE WA MA'RIFATIL A'IMMATI MIN DHURRIYYATIH\nand guided me to knowledge of him and of the Imams among his descendants;\nوَاَكْمَلْتَ بِمَعْرِفَتِهِمُ الْاِيْمَانَ وَقَبِلْتَ بِطَاعَتِهِمْ وَوِلَايَتِهِمُ الْاَعْمَالَ\nWA AKMALTA BIMA'RIFATIHIMUL EEMAANA WA QABILTA BITAA'ATIHIM WA WILAAYATIHIMUL A'MAAL\nas You have completed faith by knowledge of them, and accept deeds through obedience and loyalty to them,\nوَاسْتَعْبَدْتَ بِالصَّلَاةِ عَلَيْهِمْ عِبَادَكَ\nWASTA'BADTA BIS SALAATI A'LAYHIM I'BAADAK\nmade blessing them an act of worship for Your servants,\nوَجَعَلْتَهُمْ مِفْتَاحًا لِلدُّعَاۤءِ وَسَبَبًا لِلْاِجَابَةِ\nWA JA'ALTAHUM MIFTAAHAN LID DU'AA'I WA SABABAN LIL IJAABAH\nand made them the key to prayer and the cause of its answer:\nفَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَعَلٰى مَوْلَانَا وَسَيِّدِنَا اَبِي الْحَسَنِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ مُوْسٰى\nFASALLI A'LAYHIM AJMA'EENA WA A'LAA MAWLAANAA WA SAYYIDINAA ABIL HASANI A'LIYYIBNI MOOSAA\nbless them all, and our master and chief Abu al-Hasan Ali son of Musa,\nوَاجْعَلْنِيْ بِهِمْ عِنْدَكَ وَجِيْهًا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَمِنَ الْمُقَرَّبِيْنَ\nWAJ'ALNEE BIHIM I'NDAKA WAJEEHAN FID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI WA MINAL MUQARRABEEN\nand through them make me honoured with You in this world and the hereafter, and one of those brought near.\nوَاجْعَلْ ذُنُوْبَنَا بِهِمْ مَغْفُوْرَةً وَعُيُوْبَنَا بِهِمْ مَسْتُوْرَةً\nWAJ'AL DHUNOOBANAA BIHIM MAGHFOORATAN WA U'YOOBANAA BIHIM MASTOORAH\nThrough them make our sins forgiven and our faults covered,\nوَفَرَاۤئِضَنَا مَشْكُوْرَةً وَنَوَافِلَنَا مَبْرُوْرَةً\nWA FARAA'IDANAA MASHKOORATAN WA NAWAAFILANAA MABROORAH\nour obligatory acts appreciated and our voluntary acts approved,\nوَقُلُوْبَنَا بِذِكْرِكَ مَعْمُوْرَةً وَاَنْفُسَنَا بِطَاعَتِكَ مَسْرُوْرَةً\nWA QULOOBANAA BIDHIKRIKA MA'MOORATAN WA ANFUSANAA BITAA'ATIKA MASROORAH\nour hearts filled with remembrance of You and our souls glad in obeying You,\nوَجَوَارِحَنَا عَلٰى خِدْمَتِكَ مَقْهُوْرَةً وَاَسْمَاۤءَنَا فِيْ خَوَاۤصِّكَ مَشْهُوْرَةً\nWA JAWAARIHANAA A'LAA KHIDMATIKA MAQHOORATAN WA ASMAA'ANAA FEE KHAWAASSIKA MASH-HOORAH\nour limbs bound to Your service and our names well known among Your elect,\nوَاَرْزَاقَنَا مِنْ لَدُنْكَ مَدْرُوْرَةً وَحَوَاۤئِجَنَا لَدَيْكَ مَيْسُوْرَةً\nWA ARZAAQANAA MIN LADUNKA MADROORATAN WA HAWAA'IJANAA LADAYKA MAYSOORAH\nour provision flowing from You and our needs made easy with You,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nby Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nStand at the head and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْقَاۤئِمِ مَقَامَ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL QAA'IMI MAQAAMAL ANBIYAA'\nPeace be upon the one who stands in the place of the prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْوَارِثِ عُلُوْمَ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL WAARITHI U'LOOMAL AWSIYAA'\nPeace be upon the heir of the knowledge of the successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى خَلِيْفَةِ اللّٰهِ وَخَلِيْفَةِ رَسُوْلِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA KHALEEFATILLAAHI WA KHALEEFATI RASOOLIH\nPeace be upon the deputy of Allah and the deputy of His Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى زِمَامِ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA ZIMAAMID DEEN\nPeace be upon the rein of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نِظَامِ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA NIZAAMIL MUSLIMEEN\nPeace be upon the order of the Muslims.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى صَلَاحِ الدُّنْيَا وَعُمْدَةِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA SALAAHID DUNYAA WA U'MDATIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon the well-being of the world and the mainstay of the believers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَصْلَ الْاِسْلَامِ النَّامِيْ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ASLAL ISLAAMIN NAAMEE\nPeace be upon you, O growing root of Islam.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا فَرْعَهُ السَّامِيْ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA FAR'AHUS SAAMEE\nPeace be upon you, O its lofty branch.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ بِهٖ تَمَامُ الصَّلَاةِ وَالزَّكَاةِ وَالصِّيَامِ وَالْحَجِّ وَالْجِهَادِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN BIHEE TAMAAMUS SALAATI WAZ ZAKAATI WAS SIYAAMI WAL HAJJI WAL JIHAAD\nPeace be upon you, O you through whom prayer, zakat, fasting, hajj and jihad are made complete,\nوَتَوَفُّرِ الْفَيْءِ وَالصَّدَقَاتِ وَاِمْضَاۤءِ الْحُدُوْدِ الْمُسَمَّيَاتِ وَالْاَحْكَامِ الْمُبَيَّنَاتِ\nWA TAWAFFURIL FAY'I WAS SADAQAATI WA IMDAA'IL HUDOODIL MUSAMMAYAATI WAL AHKAAMIL MUBAYYANAAT\nand the abundance of public wealth and charity, and the carrying out of the named penalties and the explained laws.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُحَلِّلُ حَلَالَ اللّٰهِ وَالْمُحَرِّمُ حَرَامَهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUHALLILU HALAALALLAAHI WAL MUHARRIMU HARAAMAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who made lawful what Allah made lawful and forbade what He forbade.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْمُقِيْمُ حُدُوْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاَحْكَامَهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL MUQEEMU HUDOODALLAAHI WA AHKAAMAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who upheld the limits of Allah and His laws.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الذَّاۤبُّ عَنْ دِيْنِ اللّٰهِ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَالْمَوْعِظَةِ الْحَسَنَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHADH DHAABBU A'N DEENILLAAHI BIL HIKMATI WAL MAW'IZATIL HASANAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who defended the religion of Allah with wisdom and good counsel.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الدَّاعِيْ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِالْحُجَّةِ الْبَالِغَةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAD DAA'EE ILALLAAHI BIL HUJJATIL BAALIGHAH\nPeace be upon you, O you who called to Allah with the conclusive argument.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ فَضْلُهٗ كَالشَّمْسِ الْمُضِيْۤئَةِ الطَّالِعَةِ الْمُجَلِّلَةِ بِنُوْرِهَا لِلْعَالَمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN FADLUHOO KASH SHAMSIL MUDEE'ATIT TAALI'ATIL MUJALLILATI BINOORIHAA LIL A'ALAM\nPeace be upon you, O you whose excellence is like the bright rising sun that covers the world with its light.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْبَدْرُ الْمُنِيْرُ وَالسِّرَاجُ الطَّاهِرُ وَالنُّوْرُ السَّاطِعُ وَالنَّجْمُ الْهَادِيْ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL BADRUL MUNEERU WAS SIRAAJUT TAAHIRU WAN NOORUS SAATI'U WAN NAJMUL HAADEE\nPeace be upon you, O shining full moon, pure lamp, radiant light and guiding star.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عِزَّ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ وَغَيْظَ الْمُنَافِقِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA I'ZZAL MUSLIMEENA WA GHAYZAL MUNAAFIQEEN\nPeace be upon you, O might of the Muslims and vexation of the hypocrites.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بَوَارَ الْكَافِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA BAWAARAL KAAFIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O ruin of the unbelievers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا السَّادَةِ الْمَيَامِيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAS SAADATIL MAYAAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O father of the blessed masters.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ عَجَزَتْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ فَضْلِهِ الْبُلَغَاۤءُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN A'JAZAT A'N DHIKRI FADLIHIL BULAGHAA'\nPeace be upon you, O you whose excellence the eloquent are unable to recount,\nوَقَصُرَتْ عَنْ اِدْرَاكِهِ الْفُصَحَاۤءُ\nWA QASURAT A'N IDRAAKIHIL FUSAHAA'\nwhom the most fluent fall short of grasping,\nوَتَحَيَّرَتْ فِيْ نَعْتِ فَضْلِهِ الْخُطَبَاۤءُ وَلَمْ تَنْتَهِ اِلَيْهِ الْحُكَمَاۤءُ\nWA TAHAYYARAT FEE NA'TI FADLIHIL KHUTABAA'U WA LAM TANTAHI ILAYHIL HUKAMAA'\nin describing whose excellence the orators are bewildered, and whom the wise have not reached.\nذٰلِكَ فَضْلُ اللّٰهِ يُؤْتِيْهِ مَنْ يَّشَاۤءُ وَاللّٰهُ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nDHAALIKA FADLULLAAHI YU'TEEHI MAN YASHAA'U WALLAAHU DHUL FADLIL A'ZEEM\nThat is the grace of Allah, which He grants to whom He wills, and Allah is of great grace.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْلَايَ وَعَلٰۤى اٰبَاۤئِكَ الْاَكْرَمِيْنَ وَاَبْنَاۤئِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWLAAYA WA A'LAA AABAA'IKAL AKRAMEENA WA ABNAA'IKAT TAAHIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O my master, and upon your most noble forefathers and your pure children,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nThen kiss the zarih, pray the prayer of ziyarat and recite:\nيَا شَامِخًا فِيْ بُعْدِهٖ يَا رَءُوْفًا فِيْ رَحْمَتِهٖ\nYAA SHAAMIKHAN FEE BU'DIHEE YAA RA'OOFAN FEE RAHMATIH\nO You who are lofty in Your remoteness, O You who are kind in Your mercy,\nيَا مُحْيِيَ الْاَمْوَاتِ يَا مُخْرِجَ النَّبَاتِ\nYAA MUHYIYAL AMWAATI YAA MUKHRIJAN NABAAT\nO giver of life to the dead, O You who bring forth the plants,\nيَا ظَهْرَ اللَّاجِيْنَ يَا جَارَ الْمُسْتَجِيْرِيْنَ\nYAA ZAHRAL LAAJEENA YAA JAARAL MUSTAJEEREEN\nO support of those who take refuge, O protector of those who seek protection,\nيَاۤ اَسْمَعَ السَّامِعِيْنَ يَاۤ اَبْصَرَ النَّاظِرِيْنَ يَا صَرِيْخَ الْمُسْتَصْرِخِيْنَ\nYAA ASMA'AS SAAMI'EENA YAA ABSARAN NAAZIREENA YAA SAREEKHAL MUSTASRIKHEEN\nO most hearing of all who hear, O most seeing of all who see, O helper of those who cry for help,\nيَا عِمَادَ مَنْ لَا عِمَادَ لَهٗ يَا سَنَدَ مَنْ لَا سَنَدَ لَهٗ يَا ذُخْرَ مَنْ لَا ذُخْرَ لَهٗ\nYAA I'MAADA MAN LAA I'MAADA LAHOO YAA SANADA MAN LAA SANADA LAHOO YAA DHUKHRA MAN LAA DHUKHRA LAH\nO pillar of one who has no pillar, O support of one who has no support, O treasure of one who has no treasure,\nيَا حِرْزَ الضُّعَفَاۤءِ يَا كَنْزَ الْفُقَرَاۤءِ يَا عَظِيْمَ الرَّجَاۤءِ\nYAA HIRZAD DU'AFAA'I YAA KANZAL FUQARAA'I YAA A'ZEEMAR RAJAA'\nO shelter of the weak, O treasure of the poor, O You in whom hope is great,\nيَا مُنْقِذَ الْغَرْقٰى يَا مُحْيِيَ الْمَوْتٰى يَاۤ اَمَانَ الْخَاۤئِفِيْنَ يَاۤ اِلٰهَ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nYAA MUNQIDHAL GHARQAA YAA MUHYIYAL MAWTAA YAA AMAANAL KHAA'IFEENA YAA ILAAHAL A'ALAMEEN\nO rescuer of the drowning, O giver of life to the dead, O safety of the fearful, O God of the worlds,\nيَا صَانِعَ كُلِّ مَصْنُوْعٍ يَا جَابِرَ كُلِّ كَسِيْرٍ\nYAA SAANI'A KULLI MASNOO'IN YAA JAABIRA KULLI KASEER\nO maker of all that is made, O mender of all that is broken,\nيَا صَاحِبَ كُلِّ غَرِيْبٍ يَا مُؤْنِسَ كُلِّ وَحِيْدٍ\nYAA SAAHIBA KULLI GHAREEBIN YAA MU'NISA KULLI WAHEED\nO companion of every stranger, O friend of everyone alone,\nيَا قَرِيْبًا غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ يَا شَاهِدًا غَيْرَ غَاۤئِبٍ يَا غَالِبًا غَيْرَ مَغْلُوْبٍ\nYAA QAREEBAN GHAYRA BA'EEDIN YAA SHAAHIDAN GHAYRA GHAA'IBIN YAA GHAALIBAN GHAYRA MAGHLOOB\nO You who are near and not far, present and not absent, victorious and never overcome,\nيَا حَيُّ حِيْنَ لَا حَيَّ يَا مُحْيِيَ الْمَوْتٰى\nYAA HAYYU HEENA LAA HAYYA YAA MUHYIYAL MAWTAA\nO Living when there was none living, O giver of life to the dead,\nيَا حَيُّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْتَ بَدِيْعُ السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nYAA HAYYU LAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA BADEE'US SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nO Living, there is no god but You, Originator of the heavens and the earth;\nاَنْتَ الْقَاۤئِمُ عَلٰى كُلِّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ\nANTAL QAA'IMU A'LAA KULLI NAFSIN BIMAA KASABAT\nYou stand over every soul for what it has earned.\nاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI ask You to bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad\nصَلَاةً تُرْضِيْهِمْ وَتُحْظِيْهِمْ وَتُبَلِّغُهُمْ اَقْصٰى رِضَاكَ\nSALAATAN TURDEEHIM WA TUHZEEHIM WA TUBALLIGHUHUM AQSAA RIDAAK\nwith a blessing that pleases them, brings them favour and brings them to the utmost of Your good pleasure,\nوَاَنْ تَرْحَمَ ذُلِّيْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ وَتَضَرُّعِيْ اِلَيْكَ وَوَحْشَتِيْ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَاُنْسِيْ بِكَ\nWA AN TARHAMA DHULLEE BAYNA YADAYKA WA TADARRU'EE ILAYKA WA WAHSHATEE MINAN NAASI WA UNSEE BIK\nand to have mercy on my lowliness before You, my pleading with You, my estrangement from people and my intimacy with You.\nيَا كَرِيْمُ تَصَدَّقْ عَلَيَّ فِيْ هٰذِهِ السَّاعَةِ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ\nYAA KAREEMU TASADDAQ A'LAYYA FEE HAADHIHIS SAA'ATI BIRAHMATIN MIN I'NDIK\nO Generous, bestow on me in this hour a mercy from You\nتَهْدِيْ بِهَا قَلْبِيْ وَتَجْمَعُ بِهَا اَمْرِيْ وَتَلُمُّ بِهَا شَعَثِيْ\nTAHDEE BIHAA QALBEE WA TAJMA'U BIHAA AMREE WA TALUMMU BIHAA SHA'ATHEE\nby which You guide my heart, set my affairs in order and gather what is scattered in me,\nوَتُبَيِّضُ بِهَا وَجْهِيْ وَتُكْرِمُ بِهَا مَقَامِيْ وَتَحُطُّ بِهَا عَنِّيْ وِزْرِيْ\nWA TUBAYYIDU BIHAA WAJHEE WA TUKRIMU BIHAA MAQAAMEE WA TAHUTTU BIHAA A'NNEE WIZREE\nbrighten my face, honour my station and lift my burden from me,\nوَتَغْفِرُ بِهَا مَا مَضٰى مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيْ وَتَعْصِمُنِيْ بِهَا فِيْمَا بَقِيَ مِنْ عُمْرِيْ\nWA TAGHFIRU BIHAA MAA MADAA MIN DHUNOOBEE WA TA'SIMUNEE BIHAA FEEMAA BAQIYA MIN U'MREE\nforgive my past sins and protect me in what remains of my life,\nوَتَسْتَعْمِلُنِيْ فِيْ ذٰلِكَ كُلِّهٖ بِطَاعَتِكَ وَمَا يُرْضِيْكَ عَنِّيْ\nWA TASTA'MILUNEE FEE DHAALIKA KULLIHEE BITAA'ATIKA WA MAA YURDEEKA A'NNEE\nemploy me in all of it in obeying You and in what makes You pleased with me,\nوَتَخْتِمُ عَمَلِيْ بِاَحْسَنِهٖ وَتَجْعَلُ لِيْ ثَوَابَهُ الْجَنَّةَ\nWA TAKHTIMU A'MALEE BI-AHSANIHEE WA TAJ'ALU LEE THAWAABAHUL JANNAH\nseal my deeds with the best of them and make Paradise my reward for them,\nوَتَسْلُكُ بِيْ سَبِيْلَ الصَّالِحِيْنَ وَتُعِيْنُنِيْ عَلٰى صَالِحِ مَاۤ اَعْطَيْتَنِيْ\nWA TASLUKU BEE SABEELAS SAALIHEENA WA TU'EENUNEE A'LAA SAALIHI MAA A'TAYTANEE\nlead me on the path of the righteous and help me to use well what You have given me.\nوَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيْ حَاسِدًا وَلَا عَدُوًّا\nWA LAA TUSHMIT BEE HAASIDAN WA LAA A'DUWWAA\nDo not let one who envies me or an enemy gloat over me,\nوَلَا تَكِلْنِيْۤ اِلٰى نَفْسِيْ طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ اَبَدًا وَلَاۤ اَقَلَّ مِنْ ذٰلِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْثَرَ\nWA LAA TAKILNEE ILAA NAFSEE TARFATA A'YNIN ABADAN WA LAA AQALLA MIN DHAALIKA WA LAA AKTHAR\nand never leave me to myself for the blink of an eye, nor less than that nor more,\nيَا رَبَّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nYAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\nO Lord of the worlds.\nThen ask for whatever you wish. Return to the head side of the tomb and recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْ زُرْتُ هٰذَا الْاِمَامَ مُقِرًّا بِاِمَامَتِهٖ مُعْتَقِدًا لِفَرْضِ طَاعَتِهٖ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE ZURTU HAADHAL IMAAMA MUQIRRAN BI-IMAAMATIHEE MU'TAQIDAN LIFARDI TAA'ATIH\nO Allah, I have visited this Imam acknowledging his Imamate and believing in the duty to obey him.\nفَقَصَدْتُ مَشْهَدَهٗ بِذُنُوْبِيْ وَعُيُوْبِيْ وَمُوْبِقَاتِ اٰثَامِيْ\nFAQASADTU MASH-HADAHOO BIDHUNOOBEE WA U'YOOBEE WA MOOBIQAATI AATHAAMEE\nI have come to his shrine with my sins and my faults, my ruinous misdeeds,\nوَكَثْرَةِ سَيِّئَاتِيْ وَخَطَايَايَ وَمَا تَعْرِفُهٗ مِنِّيْ\nWA KATHRATI SAYYI'AATEE WA KHATAAYAAYA WA MAA TA'RIFUHOO MINNEE\nmy many evil deeds and wrongs, and all that You know of me,\nمُسْتَجِيْرًا بِعَفْوِكَ مُسْتَعِيْذًا بِحِلْمِكَ لَاجِئًا اِلٰى رُكْنِكَ عَاۤئِذًا بِرَاْفَتِكَ\nMUSTAJEERAN BI-A'FWIKA MUSTA'EEDHAN BIHILMIKA LAAJI'AN ILAA RUKNIKA A'A'IDHAN BIRA'FATIK\nseeking the shelter of Your pardon, seeking refuge in Your forbearance, taking refuge in Your support and in Your kindness,\nمُسْتَشْفِعًا بِوَلِيِّكَ وَابْنِ اَوْلِيَاۤئِكَ وَصَفِيِّكَ وَابْنِ اَصْفِيَاۤئِكَ\nMUSTASHFI'AN BIWALIYYIKA WABNI AWLIYAA'IKA WA SAFIYYIKA WABNI ASFIYAA'IK\nseeking the intercession of Your friend, son of Your friends, Your chosen one, son of Your chosen ones,\nوَاَمِيْنِكَ وَابْنِ اُمَنَاۤئِكَ وَخَلِيْفَتِكَ وَابْنِ خُلَفَاۤئِكَ\nWA AMEENIKA WABNI UMANAA'IKA WA KHALEEFATIKA WABNI KHULAFAA'IK\nYour trustee, son of Your trustees, Your deputy, son of Your deputies,\nاَلَّذِيْنَ جَعَلْتَهُمُ الْوَسِيْلَةَ اِلٰى رَحْمَتِكَ وَرِضْوَانِكَ وَالذَّرِيْعَةَ اِلٰى رَاْفَتِكَ وَغُفْرَانِكَ\nALLADHEENA JA'ALTAHUMUL WASEELATA ILAA RAHMATIKA WA RIDWAANIKA WADH DHAREE'ATA ILAA RA'FATIKA WA GHUFRAANIK\nwhom You made the means to Your mercy and good pleasure and the way to Your kindness and forgiveness.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَاُوْلٰى حَاجَاتِيْۤ اِلَيْكَ اَنْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ مَا سَلَفَ مِنْ ذُنُوْبِيْ عَلٰى كَثْرَتِهَا\nALLAAHUMMA WA OOLAA HAAJAATEE ILAYKA AN TAGHFIRA LEE MAA SALAFA MIN DHUNOOBEE A'LAA KATHRATIHAA\nO Allah, the first of my needs from You is that You forgive me my past sins, many as they are,\nوَاَنْ تَعْصِمَنِيْ فِيْمَا بَقِيَ مِنْ عُمْرِيْ\nWA AN TA'SIMANEE FEEMAA BAQIYA MIN U'MREE\nprotect me in what remains of my life,\nوَتُطَهِّرَ دِيْنِيْ مِمَّا يُدَنِّسُهٗ وَيَشِيْنُهٗ وَيُزْرِيْ بِهٖ\nWA TUTAHHIRA DEENEE MIMMAA YUDANNISUHOO WA YASHEENUHOO WA YUZREE BIH\npurify my religion of what stains it, disgraces it and lowers it,\nوَتَحْمِيَهٗ مِنَ الرَّيْبِ وَالشَّكِّ وَالْفَسَادِ وَالشِّرْكِ\nWA TAHMIYAHOO MINAR RAYBI WASH SHAKKI WAL FASAADI WASH SHIRK\nand guard it from suspicion and doubt, corruption and associating partners with You;\nوَتُثَبِّتَنِيْ عَلٰى طَاعَتِكَ وَطَاعَةِ رَسُوْلِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتِهِ النُّجَبَاۤءِ السُّعَدَاۤءِ\nWA TUTHABBITANEE A'LAA TAA'ATIKA WA TAA'ATI RASOOLIKA WA DHURRIYYATIHIN NUJABAA'IS SU'ADAA'\nthat You keep me firm in obeying You, Your Messenger and his noble and blessed descendants,\nصَلَوَاتُكَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَرَحْمَتُكَ وَسَلَامُكَ وَبَرَكَاتُكَ\nSALAWAATUKA A'LAYHIM WA RAHMATUKA WA SALAAMUKA WA BARAKAATUK\nYour blessings be upon them, and Your mercy, peace and grace;\nوَتُحْيِيَنِيْ مَاۤ اَحْيَيْتَنِيْ عَلٰى طَاعَتِهِمْ وَتُمِيْتَنِيْۤ اِذَاۤ اَمَتَّنِيْ عَلٰى طَاعَتِهِمْ\nWA TUHYIYANEE MAA AHYAYTANEE A'LAA TAA'ATIHIM WA TUMEETANEE IDHAA AMATTANEE A'LAA TAA'ATIHIM\nthat You keep me alive, for as long as You keep me alive, in obedience to them, and when You make me die, make me die in obedience to them;\nوَاَنْ لَا تَمْحُوَ مِنْ قَلْبِيْ مَوَدَّتَهُمْ وَمَحَبَّتَهُمْ\nWA AN LAA TAMHUWA MIN QALBEE MAWADDATAHUM WA MAHABBATAHUM\nand that You do not erase from my heart my affection and love for them,\nوَبُغْضَ اَعْدَاۤئِهِمْ وَمُرَافَقَةَ اَوْلِيَاۤئِهِمْ وَبِرَّهُمْ\nWA BUGHDA A'DAA'IHIM WA MURAAFAQATA AWLIYAA'IHIM WA BIRRAHUM\nmy hatred of their enemies, my companionship with their friends and my devotion to them.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ يَا رَبِّ اَنْ تَقْبَلَ ذٰلِكَ مِنِّيْ\nWA AS'ALUKA YAA RABBI AN TAQBALA DHAALIKA MINNEE\nI ask You, my Lord, to accept this from me,\nوَتُحَبِّبَ اِلَيَّ عِبَادَتَكَ وَتُبَغِّضَ اِلَيَّ مَعَاصِيَكَ\nWA TUHABBIBA ILAYYA I'BAADATAKA WA TUBAGHGHIDA ILAYYA MA'AASIYAK\nto make worshipping You dear to me and disobeying You hateful to me,\nوَتَرْزُقَنِيْ تَوْبَةً نَصُوْحًا تَرْضَاهَا وَنِيَّةً تَحْمَدُهَا وَعَمَلًا صَالِحًا تَقْبَلُهٗ\nWA TARZUQANEE TAWBATAN NASOOHAN TARDAAHAA WA NIYYATAN TAHMADUHAA WA A'MALAN SAALIHAN TAQBALUH\nand to grant me sincere repentance that pleases You, an intention You praise and a good deed You accept,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nby Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nTo bid farewell, stand facing the zarih with your back to the qiblah and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَمِيْنَ اللّٰهِ فِيْۤ اَرْضِهٖ وَحُجَّتَهٗ عَلٰى خَلْقِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEENALLAAHI FEE ARDIHEE WA HUJJATAHOO A'LAA KHALQIH\nPeace be upon you, O trustee of Allah in His earth and His proof over His creation,\nوَخَازِنَ عِلْمِهٖ وَمَوْضِعَ سِرِّهٖ وَبَابَ اَمْرِهٖ وَنَهْيِهٖ وَصِرَاطَهُ الْمُسْتَقِيْمَ\nWA KHAAZINA I'LMIHEE WA MAWDI'A SIRRIHEE WA BAABA AMRIHEE WA NAHYIHEE WA SIRAATAHUL MUSTAQEEM\ntreasurer of His knowledge, place of His secret, door of His command and prohibition, and His straight path:\nسَلَامَ مُوَدِّعٍ لَا سَئِمٍ وَلَا قَالٍ وَلَا مَالٍّ\nSALAAMA MUWADDI'IN LAA SA'IMIN WA LAA QAALIN WA LAA MAALL\nthe greeting of one bidding farewell, not out of weariness, dislike or boredom,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad,\nوَاجْعَلْ غُدُوَّنَا مَقْرُوْنًا بِالتَّوَكُّلِ عَلَيْكَ وَرَوَاحَنَا عَنْكَ مَوْصُوْلًا بِالنَّجَاحِ مِنْكَ\nWAJ'AL GHUDUWWANAA MAQROONAN BIT TAWAKKULI A'LAYKA WA RAWAAHANAA A'NKA MAWSOOLAN BIN NAJAAHI MINK\nmake our coming joined with reliance on You and our going back joined with success from You,\nوَدُعَاۤءَنَا لَكَ مَقْرُوْنًا بِحُسْنِ الْاِجَابَةِ\nWA DU'AA'ANAA LAKA MAQROONAN BIHUSNIL IJAABAH\nour prayer to You joined with a fair answer,\nوَخُضُوْعَنَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ دَاعِيًا اِلٰى رَحْمَتِكَ\nWA KHUDOO'ANAA BAYNA YADAYKA DAA'IYAN ILAA RAHMATIK\nour humility before You a call for Your mercy,\nوَاعْتِرَافَنَا بِذُنُوْبِنَا شَفِيْعًا اِلٰى عَفْوِكَ\nWA'TIRAAFANAA BIDHUNOOBINAA SHAFEE'AN ILAA A'FWIK\nand our confession of our sins an intercessor for Your pardon.\nوَارْزُقْنَا الْعَوْدَ اِلٰى زِيَارَتِهٖ ثُمَّ الْعَوْدَ اِلَيْهِ\nWARZUQNAL A'WDA ILAA ZIYAARATIHEE THUMMAL A'WDA ILAYH\nGrant us to return to visit him, and to return to him again,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nby Your mercy, O Most Merciful of the merciful.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ لَا تَجْعَلْهُ اٰخِرَ الْعَهْدِ مِنَّا لِزِيَارَةِ سَيِّدِنَا وَاِمَامِنَا الْمَفْرُوْضِ طَاعَتُهٗ عَلَيْنَا\nALLAAHUMMA LAA TAJ'ALHU AAKHIRAL A'HDI MINNAA LIZIYAARATI SAYYIDINAA WA IMAAMINAL MAFROODI TAA'ATUHOO A'LAYNAA\nO Allah, do not make this our last visit to our master and our Imam, whom You have made it our duty to obey,\nوَارْزُقْنَا زِيَارَتَهٗ اَبَدًا مَاۤ اَبْقَيْتَنَا\nWARZUQNAA ZIYAARATAHOO ABADAN MAA ABQAYTANAA\nand grant us to visit him always, for as long as You keep us alive;\nاِنَّكَ ذُو الْفَضْلِ الْعَظِيْمِ وَالْمَنِّ الْجَسِيْمِ\nINNAKA DHUL FADLIL A'ZEEMI WAL MANNIL JASEEM\nYou are the Lord of great grace and abundant favour.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA SAYYIDINAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHIT TAAHIREEN\nMay Allah bless our master Muhammad and his pure family.",
    "Imam al-Zaman (a.t.f.s.) in the Shrine\nInside the shrine of Imam al-Reza (a.s.), greet Imam al-Zaman (a.t.f.s.):\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ الزَّمَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBAZ ZAMAAN\nPeace be upon you, O Master of the Age.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَلِيْفَةَ الرَّحْمٰنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHALEEFATAR RAHMAAN\nPeace be upon you, O deputy of the All-beneficent.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا شَرِيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SHAREEKAL QUR'AAN\nPeace be upon you, O companion of the Qur’an.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا قَاطِعَ الْبُرْهَانِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA QAATI'AL BURHAAN\nPeace be upon you, O decisive proof.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اِمَامَ الْاِنْسِ وَالْجَاۤنِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA IMAAMAL INSI WAL JAANN\nPeace be upon you, O Imam of mankind and the jinn.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰۤى اٰبَاۤئِكَ الطَّيِّبِيْنَ وَاَجْدَادِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA AABAA'IKAT TAYYIBEENA WA AJDAADIKAT TAAHIREENAL MA'SOOMEEN\nPeace be upon you and upon your good fathers and your pure, sinless forefathers,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings."
