  "merits": "These forms of ziyarat of Imam Ali al-Reza (a.s.) are not in Mafatih al-Jinan. They are gathered, with the better-known forms, in the chapter on his ziyarats of al-Sahifa al-Radawiyya, compiled by Sayyid Murtada Mujtahidi Sistani. The forms Mafatih gives - the first ziyarat from Shaykh al-Saduq, al-Mufid's form, Ibn Qulawayh's salawat, Ziyarat al-Jawadiyya and the farewell - are in [Ziyarat of Imam Ali al-Reza (a.s.) — Mashhad (All Forms)](AE3).\n\nFrom al-Kitab al-Atiq al-Gharawi: Allamah al-Majlisi records this ziyarat in Bihar al-Anwar (vol. 102, pp. 49-50) from al-Kitab al-Atiq al-Gharawi, an old book of ziyarats. For the setting out, that book refers to the words it gives for setting out to visit Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) in Najaf, with the glorification to say on the way (Bihar al-Anwar, vol. 100, p. 323); they are given here in full.\n\nFrom Rawdat al-Adhkar: a ziyarat that may be recited in the shrine on any day and at any time, recorded by Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tabrizi in his Rawdat al-Adhkar, which survives only in manuscript.\n\nZiyarat of the Seven Hadith (Ziyarat-e Haft Hadith): recorded in the supplements (al-Mulhaqat) of al-Kaf'ami's al-Misbah. It takes its name from the seven narrations it quotes on the merit of visiting the Imam - from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.), Imam al-Baqir (a.s.), Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) and Imam al-Reza (a.s.) himself - which are found in Shaykh al-Saduq's Uyun Akhbar al-Rida and al-Amali. In one version of the narration from Imam al-Reza (a.s.), the reward is also of a hundred thousand martyrs and a hundred thousand of the truthful.\n\nFrom Tuhfat al-Za'ir: Allamah al-Majlisi gives this ziyarat in his Tuhfat al-Za'ir. He says it was reported by a learned scholar, probably al-Shahid, and that its words show it to come from one of the Imams (a.s.). Much of it follows the comprehensive ziyarats of all the Imams that Sayyid Ibn Tawus recorded (Bihar al-Anwar, vol. 102), addressed here to Imam al-Reza (a.s.) alone.\n\nImam al-Zaman (a.t.f.s.) in the Shrine: a short greeting to Imam al-Mahdi (a.t.f.s.) to be said inside the shrine of Imam al-Reza (a.s.), from al-Sahifa al-Mahdiyya (p. 610)."
